  "raw": {
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UMCP/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor_JR105142-1": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-14\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary Organization's Summary Statement: The Department of Philosophy at the University of Maryland, College Park, is a vibrant and research-active department with strengths across many areas of philosophy, including ethics, philosophy of mind, philosophy of language, political philosophy, metaphysics, logic, philosophy of artificial intelligence, and decision theory. The department offers undergraduate and graduate programs in Philosophy, and hosts the Philosophy, Politics, and Economics major (PPE), as well as the university’s new BA in Human-Centered Artificial Intelligence (HCAI, in collaboration with AIM). Our faculty and students pursue philosophical questions with rigor, creativity, and attention to their significance for human life, public reason, science, technology, and society. AIM is the Artificial Intelligence Interdisciplinary Institute at Maryland. Launched in 2024, it is UMD’s campus-wide hub for interdisciplinary AI research, education, and engagement. AIM brings together faculty and students across all of the university’s colleges and schools, spanning computer science and engineering, the humanities, social sciences, and other fields, with a particular commitment to responsible and ethical AI that serves the public good. The Department of Philosophy and AIM seek a tenure-track Assistant Professor or tenured Associate Professor specializing in AI Ethics and AI Safety. The successful candidate will maintain an active, innovative research program involving sustained normative and conceptual engagement with artificial intelligence, with interests broad enough to contribute across questions in AI ethics and AI safety and, ideally, with the technical literacy to engage productively with developments in AI. The successful candidate will teach and mentor undergraduates as well as graduate students in our PhD program; contribute substantially to the department’s role in HCAI, including its required technical and social cores; help develop further undergraduate and graduate offerings at the intersection of philosophy and AI; and participate in departmental, university, and professional service. Physical Demands: Normal classroom teaching demands. Minimum Qualification: Education: PHD or equivalent in Philosophy or related field by the time of appointment. Experience: 2 years of research in A.I. Ethics or A.I. Safety as primary areas of focus. Some prior teaching experience at the university level. Preference: Ability to contribute teaching relevant to the new BA program in Human-Centered AI, and in particular in the technical core. Additional Job Details Required Application Materials: Assistant-level: CV; Cover letter; Research statement; Teaching statement; Letters of recommendation (3) Associate-level: CV; Cover letter; Research statement (optional); Names of potential recommenders to be consulted if candidate is long-listed (2)   Best Consideration Date: 12/1/2026   Posting Close Date: 12/2/2026   Financial Disclosure Required No For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department ARHU-Philosophy Worker Sub-Type Faculty Regular Salary Range $127,000 - $173,000 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Faculty benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UMCP/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Assistant-Professor_JR105195": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-14\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary The Department of Cell Biology and Molecular Genetics at the University of Maryland College Park is seeking to fill a tenure-track faculty position in the broad area of cell biology. The appointment may be made at the Assistant or Associate level, commensurate with qualifications and experience. The Department is particularly interested in candidates investigating cellular mechanisms for responses to intracellular and external signals and stresses using innovative imaging, genetic, or omics approaches. The successful candidate will be expected to maintain a cutting-edge externally funded research program that synergizes with existing core groups in the department including host-pathogen interactions, genomics and gene regulation, microbial pathogenesis and immunology, virology, plant biology, and RNA structure/function. The appointed candidate will also participate in undergraduate and graduate teaching. Applicants must have a doctorate degree, an outstanding publication record, and a commitment to excellence in teaching. The department is dedicated to inclusion and ensuring that all qualified candidates have an opportunity to apply and be considered for the position. Applications should consist of (1) Cover letter, (2) Curriculum Vitae, (3) Summary of research plans (MAX two pages), (4) Teaching philosophy (one page), (5) Service Statement (one page), (6) Contact information for at least three references. www.cbmg.umd.edu If you need an accommodation in the application process, please notify errica@umd.edu Additional Job Details Minimum Requirements: Applicants must have a doctorate degree, an outstanding publication record, and a commitment to excellence in teaching. Required Application Materials: Letters should be addressed to Dr. Volker Briken, chair of the faculty search committee. (1) Cover letter (2) Curriculum Vitae (3) Summary of research plans (MAX two pages) (4) Teaching philosophy (one page) (5) Service Statement (one page) (6) Contact information for at least three references. Best Consideration Date: December 1, 2026 for best consideration, but will be accepted until the position is filled.   Posting Close Date: January 1, 2027     Financial Disclosure Required No For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department CMNS-Cell Biology & Molecular Genetics Worker Sub-Type Faculty Regular Salary Range 99,000 - 103,000 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Faculty benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
