    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UMCP/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Faculty-Assistant_JR105108-1": {
      "title": "Faculty Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-09\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary Organization's Summary Statement: The Tiwari Lab (umdwheatgenomics.weebly.com) at the University of Maryland, College Park is seeking a motivated, sharp, and hardworking Faculty Assistant (Bioinformatician) to support the lab's bioinformatics and computational needs and to help develop new tools that accelerate discovery. This role offers opportunities for co-authorship on collaborative projects while leaving room to lead independent research. Our laboratory focuses on the genomics of small grains — wheat, barley, and triticale — leveraging genomic data in the post-reference-genome era to increase resilience to biotic and abiotic stresses, improve grain quality, and reduce ecological footprint. We are passionate about advancing wheat quality and productivity, and about making our resources publicly available. If you're excited about bioinformatics, data analysis, and joining a collaborative team working on wheat genomics and crop improvement, we'd love to hear from you. Key Responsibilities: • Analyze NGS datasets (genomic, RNA-seq, Iso-Seq) for gene expression, structural variation, and functional genomics studies • Perform high-quality polyploid genome assembly and annotation using state-of-the-art methods • Conduct GWAS, QTL-seq, and MutMap analyses to identify genetic loci associated with important traits • Develop, implement, and maintain databases for managing genomic and transcriptomic datasets • Program in Python and R to build custom workflows for advanced data analysis and visualization • Run computational pipelines on Linux-based HPC systems, ensuring reproducibility of workflows • Lead individual projects from design through completion, taking ownership of timelines, methodological rigor, and the overall quality of results • Collaborate with experimental biologists to integrate bioinformatics insights into publications and grant proposals • Mentor graduate and undergraduate students in the lab as needed Physical Demands: Ability to lift and carry, able to walk long distances, bending, kneeling or stooping are standard; You are expected to work outdoors in all conditions. Unpredictable weather often forces sudden scheduling changes, requiring a highly flexible work routine. Prolonged periods sitting at a desk and working on a computer. Preferences: • Ph.D. in Bioinformatics, Computational Biology, or a related field • Strong background in NGS data analysis and genome assembly • Demonstrated experience with GWAS, QTL-seq, and MutMap pipelines • Proficiency in Python, R, and Linux/HPC environments • Proficiency in HTML and JavaScript for database development • Demonstrated ability to lead projects independently and ensure the quality and reproducibility of results • A proven publication record in computational genomics or a related field • Excellent communication and collaboration skills for multidisciplinary research Licenses/ Certifications: NA Application process interested candidates should submit: • A short, concise statement of research interests, experience, and career goals • A detailed CV • Contact information for previous mentors willing to provide recommendation letters Additional Job Details Required Application Materials: A detailed CV; A short, concise statement of research interests, experience, and career goals; Contact information for previous mentors willing to provide recommendation letters   Best Consideration Date: 10/16/2026   Posting Close Date: NA   Open Until Filled: YES   Financial Disclosure Required For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department AGNR-Plant Science & Landscape Architecture Worker Sub-Type Faculty Regular Salary Range $62,000 - $70,000 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Faculty benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UMCP/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Faculty-Specialist_JR104892": {
      "title": "Faculty Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-09\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary Organization's Summary Statement: The Women's Health Interdisciplinary Research Collaborative (WHIRC) at the University of Maryland is a campus-wide initiative to foster interdisciplinary research, educate future leaders, and inform policy and practice to improve the lives of women across their lifespan. WHIRC will support women’s health research across campus through seminars, seed funding, career development programs, and experiential learning opportunities. In addition, WHIRC will run a pilot project focused on maternal cardiovascular health in which community-engaged public health, education, and bioengineering approaches will be integrated using advanced AI. This initiative is funded through UMD's Grand Challenge initiative. WHIRC is seeking a Program Coordinator (Faculty Specialist) with strong program management, communication, and writing skills, along with a desire to apply those skills to women's health research. This position reports to WHIRC leadership and is responsible for administration, coordination, and reporting for WHIRC initiatives. The coordinator will also liaise with campus administrative units to support project activities and assist with external stakeholder outreach. Responsibilities include project management, research and logistical coordination, meeting and seminar organization, strategic communication and website management, reporting activities, and internal and external grants administration support. This is a full-time 12-month appointment, renewable for up to three years based on annual performance evaluations and continued project funding. Physical Demands: • Work is performed in a normal office environment, including the operation of standard office equipment (e.g., computer, keyboard, copier) • This position frequently presents information through oral or written communication • Minimal travel to assist with, attend, or manage meetings on and off campus Preferences: N/A Minimum Qualifications: • Bachelor's degree in health science, biological science, public health, psychology, biomedical engineering, or closely related field (Masters preferred) • Minimum 3 years of experience in research coordination, research administration, or a related academic/scientific role (experience supporting large, multi-PI sponsored research and training grant programs preferred, e.g., NIH and NSF awards) • Experience with IRB/REB protocol submissions, amendments, continuing reviews, and human subjects compliance • Strong written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to prepare technical documents, reports, and correspondence • Experience with data management and statistical analysis platforms such as Qualtrics, REDCap, SPSS, Stata, R, or equivalent • Experience in Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint) and electronic research administration systems (e.g., eRA Commons, Grants.gov) • Demonstrated ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously, prioritize tasks, and meet deadlines • Strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and accuracy in data entry, documentation, and regulatory recordkeeping • Experience with budget tracking, financial reporting, and expenditure monitoring (e.g., Workday experience preferred) • Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a multi-investigator, team-based research environment Licenses/ Certifications: N/A Additional Job Details Additional Information:  UMD will not sponsor the successful candidate for work authorization in the United States now or in the future. F1 OPT STEM support is not available for this position Required Application Materials: Resume/CV, Cover Letter, List of 3 Professional References   Best Consideration Date: 10/16/2026   Posting Close Date: N/A   Open Until Filled: Yes   Financial Disclosure Required No For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department SPHL-Family Science Worker Sub-Type Faculty Regular Salary Range $55,000 - $65,000 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Faculty benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UMCP/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Lecturer_JR105124": {
      "title": "Lecturer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-09\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary & Additional Information Organization's Summary Statement: One of 12 schools and colleges, located on the University of Maryland, College Park campus, the Robert H. Smith School of Business is a recognized leader in marketing research and education for the global economy. A comprehensive business school, Smith offers undergraduate, specialty masters, online graduate programs, full-time and part-time MBA, Executive MBA, Ph.D., and non-degree executive education programs and outreach services to the corporate community. The school is consistently ranked among the top business schools by leading business publications such as U.S. News & World Report, Financial Times, Bloomberg BusinessWeek, and The Wall Street Journal. Candidates are expected to teach undergraduate classes in marketing, including courses such as marketing principles and strategy, marketing research and analytics, digital marketing, consumer behavior, and integrated marketing communications. Candidates are expected to commit to mentoring undergraduate students in experiential projects. Physical Demands: Ability to lift ten lbs Minimum Qualifications: The ideal candidate will have a terminal degree in a related field (Ph.D. or Ed.D. is preferable) with relevant teaching experience at the undergraduate level. Preferences: All applicants are expected to demonstrate outstanding teaching skills across various subject areas in marketing and have earned a terminal degree in a related field.  Prior successful teaching in a top-ranked business school is preferred.  Licenses/ Certifications N/A Required Application Materials: Applicants should submit the following information:  A cover letter that details how their expertise and experience speak to job requirements; A current curriculum vitae; Teaching philosophy statement;  A list of recently taught courses and evidence of teaching effectiveness (i.e., teaching evaluations, awards) Names and contact information for three professional references (who will not be contacted at the initial stage of the search). Additional Information: Please address questions to the search coordinator, Ms. Laura Steeg, lsteeg@umd.edu . Review of applications will begin immediately, and early submissions are strongly encouraged. Best Consideration Date: 11/15/2026 Posting Close Date: N/A Open Until Filled: Yes  Department BMGT-Marketing Worker Sub-Type Faculty Non-Regular (Fixed Term) Salary Range $135K to $145K Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
