    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UMCP/job/TALBOT-COUNTY-EXTENSION-BUILDING/Extension-Educator--Agriculture-and-Food-Systems_JR104986": {
      "title": "Extension Educator, Agriculture and Food Systems",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-21\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary Organization's Summary Statement: University of Maryland Extension (UME) is a statewide, non-formal education system within the College of Agriculture and Natural Resources and the University of Maryland Eastern Shore. UME educational programs and problem-solving assistance are available to citizens and are based on the research and experience of land grant universities such as the University of Maryland, College Park. In Maryland, UME employs approximately 200 faculty and approximately 200 support staff and contractual employees located at the University of Maryland, College Park; University of Maryland Eastern Shore; 23 counties; Baltimore City; and four research and education centers. Many UME faculty members located on the College Park and Eastern Shore campuses have joint appointments with research and academic programs. These joint appointments promote the exchange of knowledge between the universities and among academic specialties. Position Summary/Purpose of Position: This position is located in the University of Maryland Extension (UME) Ofﬁce in Talbot County, Maryland. The position will support the Talbot County Agriculture and Food Systems Extension Program. The Educator will provide coordination and programmatic support for agronomy and horticultural crops, livestock, small farm and alternative agriculture, marketing and farm business development in Talbot County, and in collaboration with Extension faculty in the cluster and across the state. Responsibilities: • Work with UME Agriculture and Food Systems action teams to develop, promote, implement, and evaluate educational programs for agronomic and horticultural crop production, livestock production, small-scale farming and alternative agriculture enterprises, and farm and agribusiness management to provide educational opportunities for clientele related to agricultural production, business management, and marketing in Talbot County, the cluster, and across the state. • Deliver programs in crop production, farm management, integrated pest management, pesticide safety and handling, livestock production, nutrient management, ﬁnancial management, and natural resource conservation for agricultural producers in Talbot County, the cluster, and across the state. This includes support for the Talbot County Corn Club and Soybean Improvement Program. • Provide training and recertiﬁcation opportunities for certiﬁed private pesticide applicators and nutrient management voucher holders. • Develop Extension programs that improve the ﬁnancial viability of farms through cooperative and business development, grain marketing clubs, sustainable agriculture initiatives, community organization, and continuing education for producers. • Initiate and implement Extension program marketing and public relations activities, prepare information for the media, including news articles, press releases, newsletters, and social media posts. • Remain current in assigned subject matter areas and participate in relevant professional improvement opportunities. • Develop grant-funded projects to enhance and expand educational programs. • Establish and maintain strong relationships with local agricultural organizations, including attendance and participation at Talbot Soil Conservation District and Talbot County Farm Bureau; serve on city, county, and regional agricultural committees; and attend other organizational meetings as required. • Develop creative and scholarly activities that are validated by peers and communicated, such as Extension and research publications, participation in applied research, conference posters, professional presentations, and educational materials published and adopted by others. • Serve as a consultant to county government on the issues of land use, planning, and agriculture and food systems. Preferences: Qualifications: Required– • B.S. degree in agricultural education, agronomy, animal science, horticulture, agricultural business, or related ﬁeld and some experience in agricultural rural development or agribusiness. • Three years of leadership and management experience that demonstrate the ability to work well with farmers and community leaders. • Knowledge and use of computer technology for educational programming and management. • Plant diagnostic skills, such as identifying insects and diseases. • Personal transportation and valid driver’s license required. Must be willing to travel throughout the cluster, as well as the state of Maryland as needed. • Flexible work schedule required for delivering evening and weekend educational programs and activities as determined by clientele availability and needs. • Must become a certiﬁed Maryland nutrient management advisor/consultant and obtain a commercial pesticide applicators license in category-10 public agency. • This position is subject to a Criminal History Record Check. Employment is contingent upon successful completion and clearance of the Criminal History Record Check. Preferred Qualifications: • M.S. degree in agricultural education, agronomy, animal science, horticulture, agricultural business or related ﬁeld. • Extension or similar work experience in formal or non-formal community-based education. • Demonstrated ability to acquire grant funding. • Ability and experience in using social media to engage clientele. Physical Demands of the Position: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. • This position frequently presents information through vocal and written communication to individuals of various ages, socio-economic, and educational backgrounds. • A routine part of this position's responsibilities is to transport materials to and from ﬁeld research plots and teaching/event locations, including loading and unloading the vehicle. The employee will frequently lift and/or move items weighing up to 20 pounds. Set up and teardown of research machinery, project displays, and tables and chairs will be necessary at many teaching sites. • This position requires the employee to work outdoors conducting ﬁeld research, delivering programs, and teaching at events. This may occur during very hot and/or inclement weather. Able to traverse farm ﬁelds and uneven terrain. • Visual acuity is required for preparing and analyzing written or computer data and presentations. Licenses/ Certifications: n/a Additional Job Details Location: This position is located off-campus at the Talbot County Extension Office in Easton, MD. Additional Information: Candidate must be eligible to work in the United States at the time of hiring. The department will not provide sponsorship for work-visa requirements. Required Application Materials: A complete application packet must include the following documents: Cover Letter Resume Copies of Transcripts Three (3) references , each with name, mailing address, telephone number, and email address. Please note that you may upload multiple documents within the same upload field when submitting your application.   Best Consideration Date: 10/18/2026   Posting Close Date: n/a   Open Until Filled: Yes   Financial Disclosure Required No For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department AGNR-UME-Talbot Worker Sub-Type Faculty Regular Salary Range Bachelors range: $49,809 - $63,809, Masters range: $52,059 - $66,059 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Faculty benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UMCP/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Faculty-Specialist-and-Program-Director--Agricultural-Nutrient-Management-Program_JR104999": {
      "title": "Faculty Specialist and Program Director, Agricultural Nutrient Management Program",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-21\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary Organization's Summary Statement: The University of Maryland Extension's Agricultural Nutrient Management Program (ANMP), which is a component of the University of Maryland's College of Agriculture and Natural Resources, focuses on balancing nutrient applications with crop requirements to optimize crop production while reducing pollution to the Chesapeake Bay. ANMP helps farmers comply with the Water Quality Act to protect the Chesapeake Bay by promoting effective and environmentally sound nutrient application. Position Summary: The Agricultural Nutrient Management Program (ANMP) Program Director works collaboratively with the Assistant Director of Agriculture and Food Systems Extension (AgFS) to provide leadership for the ANMP which is dedicated to delivering education, research, and plan writing services in the field of agricultural nutrient management throughout Maryland. Responsibilities: • Collaborate with the AgFS Assistant Director to develop and execute the ANMP proposal and budget, manage the program, and facilitate interagency and inter-college collaborations to enhance the capacity of the University of Maryland to provide nutrient management education and services. • Work with the AgFS Assistant Director on the annual ANMP plan of work and budget in accordance with guidelines from the Maryland Department of Agriculture (MDA) and U.S. Environmental Protection Agency (EPA), within university policies and ANMP goals. • Manage the daily operations of the ANMP to provide support of university and county ANMP efforts in program management, evaluation and reporting, proposal development, training, and growth. • Strategically plan for ongoing ANMP development and innovative growth including working with University of Maryland Extension (UME) administration and federal, state, and local community partners. • Create and adapt systems for ANMP fiscal management that comply with MDA, EPA, and UMD guidelines. • Develop ANMP procedures in accordance with university policies and MDA guidelines, and communicate these policies to campus, county, and state stakeholders and educators for reporting, program development, fiscal management, and supervision of personnel. • Collaborate with the AgFS Assistant Director and ANMP Faculty Specialists to develop the required reports for MDA, EPA, and stakeholders. • Work with AgFS faculty and staff to develop statewide program design, delivery, and evaluation. • Coordinate and implement ANMP hiring procedures for ANMP staff developed in coordination with College of Agriculture and Natural Resources Human Resources (and update when necessary), UME, and the AgFS Assistant Director. • Coordinate ANMP evaluation systems and impact assessments that ensure ANMP nutrient management plans comply with MDA and EPA requirements, and UME goals, reporting systems, and impact teams. • Collaborate with the AgFS Assistant Director, the ANMP Advisory Council, and the ANMP team to develop a marketing plan to communicate ANMP impact to the university, MDA, EPA, program partners and stakeholders, and the public. • Oversee U.S. Department of Agriculture Management Evaluation reviews. Physical Demands: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. • This position frequently presents information through vocal and written communication to individuals of various ages, socio-economic, and educational backgrounds. • A routine part of this position's responsibilities is to transport materials to and from ﬁeld research plots and teaching/event locations, including loading and unloading the vehicle. The employee will frequently lift and/or move items weighing up to 20 pounds. Set up and teardown of research machinery, project displays, and tables and chairs will be necessary at many teaching sites. • This position requires the employee to work outdoors conducting ﬁeld research, delivering programs, and teaching at events. This may occur during very hot and/or inclement weather. Able to traverse farm ﬁelds and uneven terrain. • Visual acuity is required for preparing and analyzing written or computer data and presentations. Preferences: Required - Education: M.S. in soil science, agronomy, soil chemistry, nutrient management, or closely related field. Experience: • Five years of management experience in an agribusiness, higher education, non-profit, or similar field. • Demonstrated experience with budget preparation and account tracking. • Experience in personnel management, including coaching and mentoring. • Demonstrated experience in maintaining organizational policies and procedures. • This position requires the incumbent to possess personal transportation, a driver’s license valid in the State of Maryland, and the ability to travel within the state. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: • Demonstrated ability to lead and manage an organization engaged in delivering services to the public. • Ability to work independently, manage multiple priorities, communicate clearly, and interact with a variety of audiences. • Competency in the use of word processing, spreadsheet, presentation, and database software. • Working knowledge of agriculture and water quality issues. • Demonstrated teaching (extension/outreach) abilities. Preferred Qualifications: • Ph.D. in soil science, agronomy, soil chemistry, nutrient management, or closely related field. • Experience with GIS and distance education pedagogy and technology such as CANVAS, Blackboard, or Storyline. • Experience in working with volunteers, boards, councils, elected officials, and other stakeholders. • Experience acquiring extramural funds. • Certification by the MDA as a Nutrient Management Consultant. Licenses/ Certifications: Must achieve certification[DJ2.1] through the MDA as a Nutrient Management Consultant within one year of employment and maintain this certification. Additional Job Details Additional Information: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Required Application Materials: All candidates must apply online. A complete application packet must include the following documents: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae (CV) Copies of Transcripts Three (3) references , each with name, mailing address, telephone number, and email address. Please note that you may upload multiple documents within the same upload field when submitting your application.   Best Consideration Date: 10/19/2026   Posting Close Date: n/a   Open Until Filled: Yes   Financial Disclosure Required Yes For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department AGNR-UME-Special Agriculture Programs Worker Sub-Type Faculty Regular Salary Range $85,000 - $110,000 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Faculty benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UMCP/job/ARLIS-Biotechnology--Human-Performance---Multilingual-Intelligence-Research-Professional_JR104945": {
      "title": "ARLIS Biotechnology, Human Performance & Multilingual Intelligence Research Professional",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-21\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\n\nJob Description Summary Organization's Summary Statement: The Applied Research Laboratory for Intelligence & Security (ARLIS) at the University of Maryland is a University-Affiliated Research Center (UARC) dedicated to advancing research, innovation, and technology transition to improve decision making for U.S. national security. ARLIS combines deep scientific expertise with operational insight to address challenges in intelligence analysis, cybersecurity, artificial intelligence and machine learning, quantum science, and human-machine teaming. Researchers, scientists, engineers, and analysts at ARLIS collaborate with government agencies, industry partners, and academic institutions to deliver actionable insights and transformative solutions through research and development. Employees at ARLIS work on projects of critical importance, contribute directly to the nation’s security, and are supported by a culture that values integrity, collaboration, and professional growth. ARLIS is seeking qualified candidates with expertise in one or more of these technical areas to join our multidisciplinary team of research professionals: biological and antipersonnel threats, computational approaches to predicting and understanding biothreats, experience working with the Department of War and Intelligence Community (IC), novel approaches to multilingual and regional analysis, stakeholder communications, and/or complex multidisciplinary program execution. This is an evergreen requisition. We invite applicants at all experience levels whose research interests, skills, and backgrounds align with ARLIS’s Human Performance and Readiness Augmentation mission of supporting U.S. national security through intelligence-informed research on human performance, biotechnology, and readiness threats for government sponsors. Successful candidates will contribute to a portfolio of government-sponsored projects addressing emerging challenges in areas such as biological and bio-adjacent threats (including directed energy and other critical technology areas), human performance and readiness, emerging and disruptive biotechnologies, health-security issues, and the integration of multilingual and regional analysis into threat assessment and warning. Positions may include a focus on research and analysis, computational modeling of biothreats, analytic-methods and tool development, experiment and wargame design, and stakeholder engagement with IC, DoW, and allied partners. Final appointment title, level, and responsibilities will be based on candidate qualifications and matched to programmatic needs. In your cover letter, please indicate the career track (Research Specialist, Research Scientist, or Research Engineer), level, and specialization areas of greatest interest to you. Must be able to obtain a US security clearance. If selected, must meet the requirements for access to classified information and will be subject to a government security clearance investigation that includes criminal and credit history checks, as well as verification of U.S. citizenship, birth, education, employment, and military history. Final offer is contingent upon the candidate’s ability to successfully obtain the necessary interim Secret security clearance, as determined by ARLIS, prior to commencing employment. This posting is used to build a continuous pipeline of qualified candidates. Applications are reviewed on a rolling basis against current and anticipated programmatic needs. You may be contacted for an interview shortly after applying, or weeks to months later when a matching need arises. Applying to this requisition keeps your candidacy active for consideration across multiple ARLIS programs. Qualifications by Career Track and Level: Track A: Research Specialist / Faculty Specialist Entry Level (Faculty Specialist) • Bachelor’s degree. Preference given to degrees in biology, biomedical sciences, neuroscience, human factors, public health, bioengineering, technology-focused security or intelligence studies, regional/area studies, linguistics, science and technology policy, or a closely related field. • Approximately 2 years of demonstrated experience in biothreats or health-security analysis, human-performance research, intelligence or security-related research, computational analysis, or language-enabled regional analysis through work, volunteer, or extracurricular activities. • Demonstrated potential for excellence in the execution, administration, and/or management of research or academic programs. • Ability to work as part of a multidisciplinary team in a matrixed, collaborative organization. • Strong oral and written communication skills, including the ability to prepare concise briefings and written products for non-technical audiences. • Excellent analytical skills, including structured problem-solving and synthesis of qualitative and quantitative information. Mid-Level (Senior Faculty Specialist) • Master’s degree in biology, biomedical sciences, neuroscience, human factors, public health, bioengineering, technology-focused security or intelligence studies, regional/area studies, linguistics, science and technology policy, or a closely related field and 3+ years of experience in a technical, analytic, or project management role supporting defense, health-security, or intelligence programs; OR Bachelor’s degree and 5+ years of equivalent relevant experience. • Experience with emerging biothreats or biotechnology assessment, systems-level analysis of human performance and readiness, and/or planning and executing multi-stakeholder analytic projects, experiments, or wargames with scheduled deliverables. • Experience communicating and interfacing with government customers, including preparing and delivering briefings or written reports. • Knowledge of Intelligence Community, DoW, or federal health/research organizations and processes preferred. • Ability to engage key client stakeholders and work in a matrixed, collaborative organization. Track B: Research Scientist Assistant Research Scientist • Ph.D. in biology, biomedical sciences, neuroscience, human factors, public health, bioengineering, technology-focused security or intelligence studies, regional/area studies, linguistics, science and technology policy, or a closely related field • Evidence of sound scholarly or analytic production, such as peer-reviewed publications, IC or DoW reports, or equivalent high-quality products on biological threats, human performance, health-security, or related technology and regional issues. • Ability to perform R&D at a level comparable to Assistant Professor. • Expected to begin applying as PI on single-investigator proposals and serve as co-PI on larger proposals. • External recognition through awards, invited conference talks, participation in high-visibility IC/DoW/health-security exercises or panels, or equivalent. • Willingness to contribute to ARLIS and UMD citizenship (committees, internal forums, mentoring) and professional service (reviewing publications, proposals, organizing workshops). Associate Research Scientist • Ph.D. in biology, biomedical sciences, neuroscience, human factors, public health, bioengineering, technology-focused security or intelligence studies, regional/area studies, linguistics, science and technology policy, or a closely related field plus 5 years of research experience at the Assistant level or equivalent. • Significant research accomplishments with promise of continued productivity in areas such as biological and antipersonnel threats, human performance and readiness, biotechnological emerging threats, IC-focused analytic methods, or multilingual/regional analysis in support of health and readiness security. • Ability to propose, develop, and manage research projects at a level comparable to Associate Professor. • Expected to identify funding opportunities and serve as PI or co-PI on large proposals. • Growing reputation for preeminence in their specialization with commensurate external recognition. • Significant professional service contributions, including review panels for funding agencies where possible. • Regular interaction with sponsors and customers, including leading briefings and technical discussions. Full Research Scientist • Ph.D. in biology, biomedical sciences, neuroscience, human factors, public health, bioengineering, technology-focused security or intelligence studies, regional/area studies, linguistics, science and technology policy, or a closely related field plus 10 years of experience leading and performing research. • Pursues funding opportunities and serves as PI or holds primary responsibility for a significant part of a multi-investigator project. • Leads engagements with sponsors and customers, including high-level IC, DoW, and interagency stakeholders working on biotechnology, human performance, and readiness threats. • Serves in leadership roles at ARLIS and drives key initiatives and business development to grow the program. • National or international recognition as a subject matter expert with prestigious research recognitions in biothreats, human performance, biotechnology and health-security, or related domains. • Mentors students and less experienced researchers. Track C: Research Engineer Assistant Research Engineer • Master’s or Ph.D. in bioengineering, biomedical engineering, systems engineering, computer science, electrical engineering, or a related engineering field, with demonstrated interest in national security, biothreat modeling, human-performance measurement, or analytic tools for biotechnology and health-security, OR a Bachelor’s degree with equivalent relevant experience. • Evidence of ability to apply engineering methods to the design, prototyping, or evaluation of analytic tools, decision-support systems, simulation/wargaming environments, or platforms for analyzing biological and human-performance data. • Demonstrated ability to work on interdisciplinary teams and contribute to technical reports, prototypes, or experiments. • Willingness to support proposal development and customer engagement as part of a research team. Associate Research Engineer • Ph.D. plus 5 years of research experience; OR Master of Science plus 10 years of engineering research experience including success capturing and leading large projects; OR Bachelor of Science plus 15 years of relevant experience with a record of significant engineering achievement. • Initiates new projects with long-term research goals, leads work on multiple concurrent projects, and manages cross-functional engineering teams. • Serves as PI or holds primary responsibility for a significant part of a project. • Expected to identify funding opportunities and serve as PI on large proposals. • Generates significant intellectual property that may be licensed by third parties. • Mentors junior staff and participates in Professional Track promotion sub-committees. • Recognized as an authoritative subject matter expert. Full Research Engineer • Ph.D. with at least 10 years of doctoral-level research experience; OR at least 20 years of engineering research experience including success capturing and leading large projects. • Established national reputation for outstanding engineering practice, design, and development. • Pursues funding opportunities and serves as PI or holds primary responsibility for a significant part of a multi-investigator project. • Leads the design and implementation of large, multi-component projects (subcontractors, teams). • Leads engagements with sponsors and customers; builds new research programs and mission areas. • Holds leadership positions within ARLIS, on campus, or on professional committees. • Proven ability to tackle problems of considerable scope and complexity requiring novel approaches and sophisticated research techniques. • Mentors students and less experienced researchers. Physical Demands: Sedentary work performed in a normal office environment; exerts up to 10 pounds of force occasionally to move objects. Extended periods of computer-based work. Ability to attend meetings both on and off campus. Preferences: active clearance a plus and may be required for specific project Licenses/ Certifications: N/A Minimum Qualifications The appointee shall hold a Bachelor’s degree in a relevant area and show potential for excellence in the administration and/or management of academic or research programs. Faculty Specialists are expected to engage in activities such as developing curriculum and/or innovative means for delivering curriculum, supervising the non-research activities of graduate or post-doctoral students, serving as grant writers or authors of other publications for an academic or research program, conducting specialized research duties or other such duties that would generate intellectual property to which the faculty member shall retain the rights. Appointments to this rank are typically one to three years and are renewable. Additional Job Details Required Application Materials: Cover Letter, Resume, List of References   Best Consideration Date: 10/16/26   Posting Close Date: N/A   Open Until Filled: Yes   Department VPR-Applied Research Lab for Intelligence & Security Worker Sub-Type Faculty Regular Salary Range $90,000 - $210,000 Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UMCP/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Professor---Chair_JR104957": {
      "title": "Professor & Chair",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-18\nPosted: Posted 26 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary Organization's Summary Statement: The College of Education at the University of Maryland invites applications for the position of Chair of the Department of Human Development and Quantitative Methodology (HDQM). We seek a nationally or internationally recognized scholar with the vision and interdisciplinary perspective required to lead a strong and diverse faculty in its efforts to advance its tripartite mission of research, teaching, and service. The College of Education is a vibrant community advancing equitable, transformative change in schools and communities through impactful research, innovative programs and collaborative partnerships. We conduct research across education, counseling, human development and quantitative methodology, bridging research and practice while shaping education policy such as Maryland's Blueprint. We prepare equity-minded educators, counselors, psychologists and leaders through experiential, community-based learning built on strong partnerships. We foster an inclusive community that prioritizes diversity and well-being, standing as a beacon of excellence within the university's mission to transform education for good. (https://education.umd.edu/strategicplan). The 22 tenured and tenure-track faculty in the HDQM department contribute to new knowledge in developmental science, educational psychology, or quantitative methodology. Faculty members regularly receive funding from the National Institutes of Health, the National Science Foundation, the Institute of Education Sciences, many national and local foundations, and through state and federal contracts. The department's professional track faculty lead undergraduate programs, support student success, curriculum development, pedagogical innovation, and the scholarship of teaching and learning. The department is home to graduate programs in Human Development and Quantitative Methodology: Measurement and Statistics, undergraduate programs in Human Development and a major in Early Childhood/Early Childhood Special Education with dual certification (jointly administered with the Special Education Program in the Department of Counseling, Higher Education and Special Education). The Department administers the Center for Young Children, a lab school of 100 pre-school and kindergarten children with a research, practice, and training mission. The proximity to Washington DC creates unique opportunities for collaboration and impact in research, education, and policy contexts. More information about the University of Maryland, the College of Education, and the Department can be found at http://www.education.umd.edu/HDQM/. Minimum Qualifications: Education: Earned doctorate in human development, educational psychology, developmental psychology, measurement, quantitative methods, or a related area Experience: * Record of publications and funding commensurate with appointment at the rank of Professor * Administrative or leadership experience, such as serving as department chair, center director, program director/coordinator, associate dean, or other comparable roles Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: * Capacity for fiscal and human resource management * Commitment to building a collaborative and community-oriented environment * Ability to develop and support relationships across the university and community. Preferences: * Demonstrated national or international leadership and scholarship in education, human development, quantitative methodology, or a related area * A record of engaging and collaborating with stakeholders relevant to developmental science, educational psychology, and quantitative methodology * Capacity to lead with responsiveness, transparency, and fairness - building trust and shared purpose among faculty with distinct disciplinary identities * Experience in supporting and managing research centers * Evidence of creative innovations in teaching and program development * Experience with developing a vision and strategic plan * Strong record of service to the profession and the broader community Physical Demands: N/A Licenses/ Certifications: N/A Additional Job Details Required Application Materials: Candidates should upload a letter of application addressing their qualifications; current curriculum vitae; and names, titles, addresses, and telephone numbers of three persons from whom reference letters may be requested.   Best Consideration Date: 10/23/2026   Posting Close Date: 11/01/2026   Open Until Filled: No   Financial Disclosure Required For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department EDUC-College of Education Worker Sub-Type Faculty Regular Salary Range $49,655.24 - $252,288.97 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Faculty benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UMCP/job/Senior-Intelligence-Team-Lead_JR105000": {
      "title": "Senior Intelligence Team Lead",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-18\nPosted: Posted 26 Days Ago\n\nJob Description Summary Organization's Summary Statement: The Applied Research Laboratory for Intelligence & Security (ARLIS) at the University of Maryland is a University-Affiliated Research Center (UARC) dedicated to advancing research, innovation, and technology transition to improve decision making for U.S. national security. ARLIS combines deep scientific expertise with operational insight to address challenges in intelligence analysis, cybersecurity, artificial intelligence / machine learning, quantum science, and human-machine teaming. Researchers, scientists, engineers, and analysts at ARLIS collaborate with government agencies, industry partners, and academic institutions to deliver actionable insights and transformative solutions through research and development. Employees at ARLIS work on projects of critical importance, contribute directly to the nation’s security, and are supported by a culture that values integrity, collaboration, and professional growth. UMD-ARLIS is seeking qualified candidates for the Analytic Team Lead role, with expertise in leading all-source analytic teams and research programs. Candidates must have prior experience serving as an intelligence analyst for a U.S. Government all-source agency. Preferred candidates will have experience working as a Branch Chief, Senior Intelligence Analyst (SIA), or in the Senior Analytic Service (SAS) for an all-source U.S. Government Agency. Ideal candidates will have a background in assessing critical and emerging technologies and their implications for national and economic security. Candidates should also be able to demonstrate the ability to conduct interdisciplinary research at the intersection of people, policy, and technology. Successful candidates will contribute to a portfolio of government-sponsored projects addressing emerging challenges in areas such as technology assessment, technology transition and adoption, risk and resilience, governance and policy, and human and organizational factors shaping technology use. Work may include research development, rapid analytic sprints, stakeholder engagement, and the production of actionable insights that inform decision-making across technology strategy, acquisition, and operational planning. Positions may include a focus on applied research, systems-level analysis, policy-relevant technical assessment, and/or field-informed studies of how technologies are used in real-world contexts. Final appointment title and responsibilities will be based on qualifications and matched to programmatic needs. Roles and Responsibilities: Roles and Responsibilities will vary by project and candidate expertise and may include: • Managing teams conducting interdisciplinary research on critical and emerging technologies at the intersection of people, policy, and technology, with an emphasis on national and economic security relevance • Guiding assessments of technology capabilities, limitations, and trajectories across a family of technologies, including second- and third-order impacts on missions, markets, and society • Analyzing socio-technical adoption and use, including how individuals, organizations, and institutions interact with technologies and how policy and governance shape their evolution • Running an analytic program that evaluates technology ecosystems, supply chains, and economics (e.g., production scaling, chokepoints, dependencies, investments, and market structure) that influence technology development and strategic risk • Contributing to research proposals and technical work plans, including scoping key intelligence questions, defining methods, and supporting sponsor engagement as needed • Collaborating with interdisciplinary teams including engineers, data scientists, domain experts, behavioral and social scientists, and policy analysts to integrate methods and findings • Editing and Preparing finished intelligence products and briefings for government stakeholders, translating complex analyses into clear, decision-relevant products (e.g., reports, slide briefings, memos, and research summaries) • Developing and mentoring junior researchers or researchers with minimal previous experience applying IC analytic tradecraft to become self-sufficient, full-performance all-source analysts Must be able to obtain a U.S. security clearance. If selected, you must meet the requirements for access to classified information and will be subject to a government security clearance investigation that includes criminal and credit history checks, as well as verification of U.S. citizenship, birth, education, employment, and military history. Minimum Qualifications: ARLIS is hiring at the Principal Faculty level for the Research Specialist track. In addition to a proven record of excellence in managing and directing an academic or research program, the appointee shall hold a Ph.D. or have at least 5 years of full-time experience as a Senior Faculty Specialist, or its equivalent. • Experience conceptualizing and editing finished intelligence products for senior U.S. Government policymakers or DoW officials. • Superior ability to deliver excellence in the execution, administration, and/or management of research or analytic programs • Proven knowledge of IC writing tradecraft and experience teaching others about this discipline • Lead engagements with U.S. government sponsors, customers, and stakeholders • Ability to work as part of a multi-disciplinary opportunity capture team in a matrixed organization with a collaborative and team-centric culture • Strong oral and written communication skills Ability to: • Initiate new projects with long-term research goals and lead work on multiple, concurrent projects while managing cross-functional teams • Serve as Principal Investigator or having primary responsibility for a significant part of a project • Interact and lead engagement with U.S. government sponsors, customers, and stakeholders • Identify funding opportunities and serve as Principal Investigator on large proposals • Mentor junior staff and Professional Track Faculty Specialists and participating in their promotion sub-committees Physical Demands: Sedentary work performed in a normal office environment; exerts up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects, including the human body. Ability to attend meetings both on and off campus. Spending long hours in front of a computer screen. Preferences: •Active TS/SCI security clearance • Ph.D. or Master’s degree in a relevant field such international affairs, economics, political science, basic science, engineering, public policy, or related discipline and 8+ years of experience as an all-source analyst for a U.S. Government Agency or similar; or Bachelor's degree and 10+ years of relevant experience. • Experience working as a Branch Chief, Senior Intelligence Analyst (SIA), or in the Senior Analytic Service (SAS) for an all-source U.S. Government Agency. Prior experience as a GS/GG-14 or equivalent all-source analyst will also be considered. Licenses/ Certifications: N/A Minimum Qualifications In addition to a proven record of excellence in managing and directing an academic or research program, the appointee shall hold a Ph.D. or have at least 5 years of full-time experience as a Senior Faculty Specialist, or its equivalent. Appointments are typically made as five-year contracts. Additional Job Details Required Application Materials: Cover Letter, Resume, List of References   Best Consideration Date: N/A   Posting Close Date: 11/30/26   Open Until Filled: Yes   Department VPR-Applied Research Lab for Intelligence & Security Worker Sub-Type Faculty Regular Salary Range $160,000 - $220,000 Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UMCP/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Non-Kinetic-Effects-Software-and-AI-ML-Applications-Specialist_JR104955": {
      "title": "Non-Kinetic Effects Software and AI/ML Applications Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-14\nPosted: Posted 30 Days Ago\n\nJob Description Summary Organization's Summary Statement: The Applied Research Laboratory for Intelligence & Security (ARLIS) at the University of Maryland is a University-Affiliated Research Center (UARC) dedicated to advancing research, innovation, and technology transition to improve decision making for U.S. national security. ARLIS combines deep scientific expertise with operational insight to address challenges in intelligence analysis, cybersecurity, artificial intelligence / machine learning, quantum science, and human-machine teaming. Researchers, scientists, engineers, and analysts at ARLIS collaborate with government agencies, industry partners, and academic institutions to deliver actionable insights and transformative solutions through research and development. Employees at ARLIS work on projects of critical importance, contribute directly to the nation’s security, and are supported by a culture that values integrity, collaboration, and professional growth. This is an evergreen requisition for Non-Kinetic Effects Software and AI/ML Applications Specialists at the Faculty Research Specialist (FRS) and Senior Faculty Research Specialist (Senior FRS) ranks. The Specialist supports ARLIS’s expanding research portfolio in operation innovation and information. The role will contribute to a portfolio of government-sponsored projects that integrate information warfare, open-source intelligence (OSINT), and foreign languages into integrated modeling & simulation (M&S) and artificial intelligence (AI) applications. The role supports application development to support sponsor non-kinetic effect decision support system needs as well as enabling ongoing research via Agentic AI into these areas. Applications are reviewed on a rolling basis against current and anticipated programmatic needs; candidates may be contacted shortly after applying or weeks to months later when a matching need arises. Final appointment title and responsibilities will be based on qualifications and matched to programmatic needs. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: - Experience in Python or other modern object-oriented coding language. - Skill in the use of Microsoft Office products. - Skill in troubleshooting system errors. - Ability to multi-task and prioritize assignments. - Ability to analyze situations and determine the best recourse for response. Must be able to obtain a US security clearance. If selected, must meet the requirements for access to classified information and will be subject to a government security clearance investigation that includes criminal and credit history checks, as well as verification of U.S. citizenship, birth, education, employment, and military history. Final offer is contingent upon the candidate’s ability to successfully obtain the necessary interim Secret security clearance, as determined by ARLIS, prior to commencing employment. Faculty Research Specialist (FRS): The FRS supports the development of non-kinetic effects software, M&S, and AI/ML applications under the direction of project leads. At this rank the Specialist integrates onto Agile project teams; implements and tests application components, data pipelines, and M&S modules in Python or other modern object-oriented languages; assists in setting up AI tools and Agentic AI harnesses that enable research tasks for scientists; documents code and deliverables; and learns ARLIS processes and policies, with the expectation of growing toward increasingly independent contribution. Senior Faculty Research Specialist (Senior FRS): The Senior FRS brings a well-developed, specialized skill set in software development, Agentic AI, and M&S and a demonstrated ability to administer research and development tasks, as evidenced by experience successfully discharging responsibilities such as those of a Faculty Research Specialist. At this rank the Specialist owns end-to-end application development from design through deployment, works with project leads to design enabling systems and research plans, presents results at internal and external research forums, participates in the pursuit and development of proposals, and mentors and trains new Faculty Research Specialists and students. Minimum Qualifications Education: Faculty Research Specialist: Bachelor’s Degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Information Science, Data Science, or a related field from an accredited college or university. Senior Faculty Research Specialist: Master’s Degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Information Science, Data Science, or a related field from an accredited college or university, or a Bachelor’s Degree in one of these fields combined with the additional experience listed below. Experience: Programming experience in Python or other modern object-oriented languages, with exposure to AI/ML frameworks (TensorFlow, PyTorch, scikit-learn) and understanding of machine learning fundamentals. Faculty Research Specialist: Demonstrated potential for excellence in application development in support of research, such as through academic projects, research assistantships, internships, or prior software development roles. No additional years of experience are required beyond the degree. Senior Faculty Research Specialist: Master’s Degree plus 3 years of research or applications development experience, OR Bachelor’s Degree plus at least 5 years of full-time experience at the Faculty Research Specialist level or in roles of equivalent responsibility. Superior ability to administer research and development tasks, as evidenced by experience successfully discharging responsibilities such as those of a Faculty Research Specialist (e.g., delivering application components as a core member of an Agile project team), and evidence of technical contributions (e.g., delivered software, published code, technical reports, or sponsor deliverables). Physical Demands: Sedentary work performed in a normal office environment; exerts up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects, including the human body. Ability to attend meetings both on and off campus. Spending long hours in front of a computer screen. Preferences: Education: Master’s Degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Information Science, Data Science, or a related field (Faculty Research Specialist rank). Experience: - 3+ years of experience in Python or other modern object-oriented languages, with exposure to Agentic AI platforms and understanding of machine learning fundamentals. - Prior experience in supporting non-kinetic technical applications or software tools for national security uses. - 1+ years in AI-assisted programming (e.g. Codex etc.). - Prior experience in Cloud architectures and deployments. - Prior experience in virtualization deployment including Dockers. - Programming experience in R or other statistical or quantitative research applications. - Experience with developing M&S either via agent-based modeling (ABM) platforms such as Mesa, system dynamics platforms such as Stella or Vensim, or other equivalent M&S experience. - Experience linking Agentic AI and M&S applications through API development. - Prior experience in adjacent development skills including front-end development, UI/UX design, advanced data science, and/or quantitative statistic programs is a plus. - Comfort working independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced, evolving environment. - Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. - Experience in supporting AI/ML research from a coding and application development perspective. - Active, or eligible for a security clearance; prior clearance at SECRET or higher that is active or inactive is preferred; current TS/SCI clearance strongly preferred. - Experience mentoring or training junior developers, researchers, or students (Senior Faculty Research Specialist). Licenses/ Certifications: N/A Minimum Qualifications In addition to a proven record of excellence in managing and directing an academic or research program, the appointee shall hold a Ph.D. or have at least 5 years of full-time experience as a Senior Faculty Specialist, or its equivalent. Appointments are typically made as five-year contracts. Appointments for additional five-year terms can be renewed as early as the third year of any given five-year contract. Additional Job Details Required Application Materials: Cover Letter, Resume, List of References   Best Consideration Date: 10/16/26   Posting Close Date: N/A   Open Until Filled: Yes   Department VPR-Applied Research Lab for Intelligence & Security Worker Sub-Type Faculty Regular Salary Range $70,000 - $140,000 Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UMCP/job/Test-and-Evaluation--T-E--Research-Professional_JR104947": {
      "title": "Test and Evaluation (T&E) Research Professional",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-14\nPosted: Posted 30 Days Ago\n\nJob Description Summary Organization's Summary Statement: The Applied Research Laboratory for Intelligence & Security (ARLIS) at the University of Maryland is a University-Affiliated Research Center (UARC) dedicated to advancing research, innovation, and technology transition to improve decision making for U.S. national security. ARLIS combines deep scientific expertise with operational insight to address challenges in intelligence analysis, cybersecurity, artificial intelligence / machine learning, quantum science, and human-machine teaming. Researchers, scientists, engineers, and analysts at ARLIS collaborate with government agencies, industry partners, and academic institutions to deliver actionable insights and transformative solutions through research and development. Employees at ARLIS work on projects of critical importance, contribute directly to the nation’s security, and are supported by a culture that values integrity, collaboration, and professional growth. The Test and Evaluation (T&E) Research Professional serves ARLIS by conducting T&E of emerging, intelligent technologies, especially those with implications for national and economic security. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: • Ability to conduct research to assess, including verify and validate, novel technologies through the design, execution, analysis, and documentation of appropriately rigorous T&E methods and activities. • Ability to engage stakeholders (e.g., USG personnel, technology developers, end-users) to extract respective preferences. • Skill in the development and execution of both formative and summative evaluations at one or more technology levels (e.g., component, capability, system levels). • Skill in working within collaborative, multi-disciplinary teams and communicating complex topics through technical deliverables and briefings for U.S. Government stakeholders. Must be able to obtain a U.S. security clearance. If selected, you must meet the requirements for access to classified information and will be subject to a government security clearance investigation that includes criminal and credit history checks, as well as verification of U.S. citizenship, birth, education, employment, and military history. Final offer is contingent upon the candidate’s ability to successfully obtain the necessary interim Secret security clearance, as determined by the U.S. Government, prior to commencing employment Research Specialist Qualifications: Entry Level: ● Bachelor’s degree plus 2 years of demonstrated experience in supporting / contributing to T&E-related efforts through volunteer, extracurricular, or work activities. Mid Level: ● Master’s degree plus 3+ years of experience in a technical role or project management position for defense or intelligence T&E programs with experience in technical requirements discovery, performance metric articulation, T&E design, technology verification and validation, performance assessment analysis, executing on technical programs with scheduled deliverables, and communicating and interfacing with government customers; or Bachelor’s degree plus 5+ years of relevant experience in a role of equivalent responsibility. Senior Level: ● Master’s degree plus 7+ years of experience in a technical role or project management position for defense or intelligence T&E programs with experience in technical requirements discovery, performance metric articulation, T&E design, technology verification and validation, performance assessment analysis, executing on multiple technical programs with scheduled deliverables, and communicating and interfacing with government customers; or Bachelor’s degree plus 10+ years of relevant experience in a role of equivalent responsibility. Research Engineer Qualifications: ● PhD plus 5 years or more of relevant T&E research (design, execution, analysis) experience, depending on level, including success leading research projects and interacting with government sponsors, customers, and stakeholders. ● Demonstrated potential for excellence in the execution, administration, and/or management of research or academic programs. ● Ability to work as part of a multi-disciplinary team in a matrixed organization with a collaborative and team-centric culture. ● Strong oral and written communication skills. ● Excellent analytical and deep-dive skills. Preferences: ● Degree in Mechanical Engineering, Systems Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Industrial Engineering, Manufacturing Engineering or a related field ● Experience designing test plans to assess (both verification and validation) emerging technologies at multiple levels (i.e., component, capability, system) including identifying appropriate measures and metrics, developing appropriate use cases/test scenarios, and developing a data collection strategy ● Experience executing T&E exercises and analyzing T&E data to draw meaningful, actionable conclusions ● Experience documenting T&E efforts including lessons learned, to provide necessary insight to project sponsors and collaborators to enable informed decision-making ● Experience documenting the current-state-of-the-art including best practices and pain points ● Experience building out over-arching formative T&E plans that would enable multiple test events to support the maturation of an emerging technology ● Experience developing and deploying measurement tools (e.g., physical sensors, software instrumentation) to gather T&E-purposed performance measures and metrics ● Experience preparing technical deliverables and briefings for government stakeholders. ● Experience contributing to research proposals and technical work plans, including scoping technical approaches, defining methods, estimating effort, and identifying risks. ● Comfort working independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced, evolving environment ● Strong organizational skills and attention to detail ● Active or eligible for a security clearance Physical Demands: Sedentary work performed in a normal office environment; exerts up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects, including the human body. Ability to attend meetings both on and off campus. Spending long hours in front of a computer screen. Licenses/ Certifications: N/A Minimum Qualifications The appointee shall hold a Bachelor’s degree in a relevant area and show potential for excellence in the administration and/or management of academic or research programs. Faculty Specialists are expected to engage in activities such as developing curriculum and/or innovative means for delivering curriculum, supervising the non-research activities of graduate or post-doctoral students, serving as grant writers or authors of other publications for an academic or research program, conducting specialized research duties or other such duties that would generate intellectual property to which the faculty member shall retain the rights. Appointments to this rank are typically one to three years and are renewable. Additional Job Details Required Application Materials: Cover Letter, Resume, List of References   Best Consideration Date: 10/16/26   Posting Close Date: N/A   Open Until Filled: Yes   Department VPR-Applied Research Lab for Intelligence & Security Worker Sub-Type Faculty Regular Salary Range $49,072 - $252,288 Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UMCP/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Assistant-Clinical-Professor_JR104869": {
      "title": "Assistant Clinical Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-14\nPosted: Posted 30 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary Organization's Summary Statement: The University of Maryland, College Park, an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer, complies with all applicable federal and state laws and regulations regarding nondiscrimination and affirmative action; all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. The University is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all persons and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, physical or mental disability, protected veteran status, age, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, creed, marital status, political affiliation, personal appearance, or on the basis of rights secured by the First Amendment, in all aspects of employment, educational programs and activities, and admissions. Physical Demands: Able to take office and classroom tasks, ability to sit for extended hours, visual acuity to read data on reports and computer screens, ability to type on keyboard for extended periods. Additional Job Details The Department of Epidemiology and Biostatistics, School of Public Health, University of Maryland, College Park (http://www.sph.umd.edu/EPIB) invites applications for an Assistant Clinical Professor in biostatistics. The position primarily involves teaching courses along with departmental related duties/service. The Department’s mission is to improve health and reduce health disparities in local communities, the state of Maryland, and the nation. The Department offers an MPH degree in biostatistics, a PhD degree in biostatistics and bioinformatics (jointly offered with the Department of Mathematics), an MPH degree in epidemiology, and a PhD degree in epidemiology. The School of Public Health is accredited by the Council on Education for Public Health and is located on the flagship campus of the University of Maryland. The School’s vision is “to be a leader in the discovery, application and dissemination of public health knowledge in the State of Maryland, the nation and the world.” The successful candidate will contribute to fulfilling this vision. QUALIFICATIONS. Qualified candidates should possess a doctoral degree in biostatistics or a closely related public health field. Qualified candidates will have demonstrated the ability to teach undergraduate and graduate level biostatistics courses and mentor students. RESPONSIBILITIES. Successful candidates for the position are expected to teach biostatistics courses to undergraduate and graduate students at fundamental and intermediate levels, mentor students, and engage in university and professional service. Effective interpersonal, communication, and collaborative skills are essential. SALARY and APPOINTMENT DATE. This is a full-time, nine-month, non-tenure-track position with benefits; salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. Funding is guaranteed for 9 months annually, with the potential to extend salary support with teaching summer courses. The initial contract length is 1 year with possible future renewable multi-year contracts. Appointments may begin January 2027 or a mutually agreed-upon date. APPLICATION. For best consideration, candidates should submit materials by October 2, 2026. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Applications should include the following: 1) cover letter clearly indicating how the candidate meets the qualifications listed above, 2) curriculum vitae, 3) teaching statements, and 4) contact information for three references (to be contacted only with the candidate’s approval). The Department of Epidemiology and Biostatistics is committed to increasing the diversity of the campus community. Candidates who have experience working with a diverse range of faculty, staff, and students, and who can contribute to the climate of inclusivity are encouraged to state their experiences in these areas. Contact: Dr. Charles Ma, Search Committee Chair (tma0929@umd.edu) for questions about the position, and Ms. Bernadette Gormally(bgormall@umd.edu) for questions about application submission. A wide range of collaborative opportunities exist at the University with nearby federal, state and local government agencies, non-profit organizations, and other academic institutions. Collaborative efforts have been made to bring together statisticians from both College Park and Baltimore campuses of the University of Maryland. Statisticians in our Department participate in the new Applied Statistics concentration of the Applied Mathematics, Statistics and Scientific Computation (AMSC) Program. Our faculty members also interact with faculty in the Joint Program in Survey Methodology (JPSM), the Maryland Population Research Center (MPRC), the Global Environmental and Occupational Health (GEOH), the Biostatistics and Risk Assessment Center (BRAC), the Center for Bioinformatics and Computational Biology (CBCB), University of Maryland School of Medicine at Baltimore, as well as with researchers in other applied fields. The position represents a unique opportunity to join a growing department and contribute to an exciting research agenda and graduate student training program. The University of Maryland is a Research Intensive University. College Park is the flagship campus of the University of Maryland System with over 2,500 faculty and 30,000 undergraduate and 11,000 graduate students. The University is located 8 miles from Washington D.C. For further information on the University of Maryland, please visit the University Web Site: http://www.umd.edu. Required Application Materials: 1 - Cover letter clearly indicating how the candidate meets the qualifications listed above 2 - curriculum vitae 3 - teaching statements 4 - contact information for three references (to be contacted only with the candidate’s approval)   Best Consideration Date: 10/02/2026   Posting Close Date: NA   Open Until Filled: Yes   Financial Disclosure Required No For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department SPHL-Epidemiology & Biostatistics Worker Sub-Type Faculty Regular Salary Range The salary range: 85,000 - 95,000 9-month position Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Faculty benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UMCP/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Investigative-Journalism-Professor-and-Investigations-Editor_JR104857": {
      "title": "Investigative Journalism Professor and Investigations Editor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-10\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary Organization's Summary Statement: The Philip Merrill College of Journalism at the University of Maryland, consistently ranked among the world's top journalism schools, develops journalists and media scholars with rigorous reporting, research and analytical skills, a commitment to ethics, and an appreciation for the First Amendment’s key role in a free society. Located a few miles from Washington, D.C., the college prepares students for a dynamic profession, with a faculty that includes acclaimed researchers and repeat winners of journalism’s top awards — including the Pulitzer, Peabody and Emmy awards. Merrill College students enjoy small classes and also have access to the resources and opportunities available at one of the nation's top public research universities. Our students leave the university with strong writing and visual skills, a command of technology and a nuanced understanding of data analysis, AI and audience engagement. The college has approximately 450 undergraduate and graduate students, and about 60 faculty and staff. The college is housed in Knight Hall, located on the UMD College Park campus. The college also runs news bureaus in Annapolis and Washington, is the home of the award-winning Howard Center for Investigative Journalism, The Shirley Povich Center for Sports Journalism and the Local News Network. It is also host to the national office of the National Association of Black Journalists. Overview The University of Maryland Philip Merrill College of Journalism is seeking an experienced investigative journalist to join its faculty as an investigative journalism professor. This person will also serve as the Howard Center for Investigative Journalism’s lead investigations editor.     The Howard Center is an investigative reporting unit and journalism training program based at the University of Maryland’s Philip Merrill College of Journalism. Funded by the Scripps Howard Foundation, it regularly partners with major national newsrooms — such as NPR, PBS NewsHour, KFF Health News and the Organized Crime and Corruption Reporting Project — to produce deeply reported investigations. The center, founded in 2019, specializes in investigative reporting that incorporates complex data and digital document analysis, advanced computational methods, and, increasingly, visual forensic and open source intelligence (OSINT) reporting techniques. In a partnership with the Associated Press global investigations team and a FRONTLINE (PBS) documentary unit, the center was named a finalist for the Pulitzer Prize in Investigative Reporting in 2025 for an in-depth, data-driven investigation into police custody deaths. The center has also won dozens of major journalism awards for its investigations, including two Edward R. Murrow Awards, a National Headliner Award and an IRE Medal.  Job Title and Other Details This position is a full-time, year-round, in-person position based in the Howard Center in College Park, Maryland. It is not eligible for a fully remote or hybrid schedule, although occasional remote work is allowed.   This position is posted as an “open rank” position. We expect to hire this person as a “Professor” or “Associate Professor” — formal University of Maryland titles that provide tenure — or as a “Lecturer” or “Professor of the Practice” — titles that do not provide tenure or eligibility for tenure in the future. If this person’s record of professional accomplishment meets or exceeds the university’s high standards for appointment as an “Associate Professor” or “Professor” with tenure, we expect to appoint them to that position. If it does not, we expect to appoint them as a “Lecturer” or “Professor of the Practice” on a five-year renewable contract.    Minimum Requirements Applicants must have:  A bachelor’s degree. A minimum of 5 years of experience working as a journalist.  Experience producing investigative journalism as a reporter.  Experience managing complex investigative journalism projects as an editor.  Additional Job Details Responsibilities This person will work full time as investigations editor in the Howard Center. In that role, they will: Serve as lead editor on investigative reporting projects produced by Howard Center graduate fellows and undergraduate students, working with Merrill College faculty, professional newsroom partners and partners at other journalism schools.   Teach one course per semester — a total of two courses per year — that are directly integrated with Howard Center investigations. This includes a foundational Howard Center investigative reporting methods course and an intensive, multiday Howard Center investigative reporting capstone course. Work with the Howard Center director to identify, establish and manage partnerships with professional newsrooms and manage projects. Preferred Experience We expect successful candidates to bring some of the experiences listed below. No candidate is expected to have all of them. We are looking for someone who can demonstrate relevant experience in some of these areas, while articulating a clear interest in the others: Teaching and mentoring experience, which could include university-level teaching or consistently running workshops at professional conferences like IRE and NICAR. Experience working with data journalists on data-driven investigative projects and an openness to experimenting with new reporting methods that incorporate artificial intelligence and open source intelligence. Experience leading or participating in investigative collaborations involving multiple newsrooms.   Experience with long-form writing and editing. Experience with — or a clear interest in learning — storytelling forms tailored to reach new audiences on multiple platforms.  Application Materials  A CV  A cover letter in which you:  Succinctly explain your interest in the position.   Explain, with specifics, how your experience and interests align with the listed responsibilities, requirements and preferred experiences.  Links to three examples of your work, along with a brief explanation of your role in their production.  Benefits The position has excellent State of Maryland benefits, including: 41 days of leave per year (22 vacation days, 3 personal days, 16 holidays) and 15 days of sick leave per year.  A choice of a defined-benefit retirement plan (a State of Maryland pension) or a defined-contribution retirement plan — the public sector equivalent of a 401(k) — with a generous employer contribution (employer contributes an extra 7.25% of salary, with no employee contribution required to receive it).  Excellent State of Maryland benefits (individual, spouse and dependent) for healthcare, prescription drugs, dental, vision, term-life, accidental death and long-term disability. Tuition remission at the University of Maryland, College Park, and other University System of Maryland schools for faculty and their dependents.  Up to 12 weeks of paid parental leave. Additional benefit details here: https://uhr.umd.edu/benefits-and-wellness Physical Demands: N/A   Best Consideration Date: 9/30/2026 Posting Close Date: 01/10/2027 Open Until Filled: Yes Financial Disclosure Required For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department JOUR-Philip Merrill College of Journalism Worker Sub-Type Faculty Regular Salary Range 160,000-185,000 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Faculty benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UMCP/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Assistant-Professor_JR103903": {
      "title": "Open Rank - Assistant / Associate / Full Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary ORGANIZATION'S SUMMARY STATEMENT This full-time, tenure-track faculty position is in the Department of Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering within the A. James Clark School of Engineering at the University of Maryland, College Park (www.chbe.umd.edu). The position is responsible for developing and sustaining an impactful, externally funded research program; teaching and mentoring both graduate and undergraduate students; and contributing to the department’s collaborative culture and broader mission. This includes strong scholarly work, innovative instruction at both the graduate and undergraduate levels, participation in faculty governance and institution-building, service to the broader scientific community, and building partnerships within the department, the A. James Clark School of Engineering and the university, as well as with industrial, governmental, or community partners. Founded in 1856, the University of Maryland, College Park, is the flagship institution in the University System of Maryland. Our 1,250-acre College Park campus is just minutes away from Washington, D.C., and the nexus of the nation’s legislative, executive, and judicial centers of power. This unique proximity to business and technology leaders, federal departments and agencies, and a myriad of research entities, embassies, think tanks, cultural centers, and non-profit organizations is simply unparalleled. Synergistic opportunities for our faculty and students abound and are virtually limitless in the nation’s capital and surrounding areas. The University is located close to NSF, NIH, and other funding agencies, and has strong research ties with government research labs (DoD, NIST, etc.), corporations, and start-ups. The Washington DC area has three major airports and a vibrant culture, is reachable by metro, and has primary and secondary schools that are among the best in the nation. Notable Facts for Department, College, and University: ● The Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering Department (ChBE) currently consists of 17 tenure/tenure-track faculty ● The College received a significant gift from the A. James &amp; Alice B. Clark Foundation of $220M. This includes funding to assist faculty and attract and fund first-year PhD students. ● The A. James Clark School of Engineering has added or will be completing several new buildings (Clark Hall and Zupnik Hall) that offer expansive lab space, innovation labs for capstone design projects, and a quantum technology center. ● UMD is a leader in Quantum Computing (quantum.umd.edu) that partners with leaders in the computing industry and government. ● UMD is also a leader in Artificial Intelligence (ai.umd.edu) with a recently formed center Artificial Intelligence Interdisciplinary Institute at Maryland (AIM) The A. James Clark School of Engineering at the University of Maryland catalyzes high-quality research, innovation, and learning, preparing our students to create innovations that will address the 21st century Grand Challenges (e.g., energy, environment, security, and human health) and improve the human condition. The Clark School is dedicated to leading and transforming the engineering discipline and profession, accelerating entrepreneurship, and transforming research and learning activities into innovations that benefit millions. PHYSICAL DEMANDS ● Lift 5lbs - 10lbs ● Using a computer and keyboard ● Sitting for periods of time ● Standing for periods of time ● Using lab or mechanical equipment ● Use of non-flammable gas ● Use of non-toxic chemicals ● Bending ● Kneeling ● Twisting (head or neck) ● No unusual physical or environmental demands. LICENSES/ CERTIFICATIONS N/A Additional Job Details Preferences: Candidates will be expected to establish a creative, well-funded, and collaborative research program that will serve to educate graduate and undergraduate students and advance their field.  Candidates should be effective communicators and have the ability and interest to work with student populations from a variety of backgrounds, learning styles, and skill levels. The successful candidate will contribute to the teaching of undergraduate and graduate courses within the department. Postdoctoral training beyond the Ph.D. is viewed as providing additional training needed to be successful as an Assistant / Associate / Full Professor, but it is not mandatory. Additional Information: Open Until Filled: Yes For best consideration, applications should be submitted by Dec 1, 2026. The review of applications will begin on Dec 2, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. The following  materials/documents are required for an application: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Statement of Research Statement of Teaching Interests Minimum of (3) professional references with contact information (Company/Agency/Institution, phone, email address) Note: For candidates who hold BS degrees outside of chemical engineering, the teaching statement should address their ability to teach core undergraduate courses in ChBE. A link to the candidates’ Google Scholar, Web of Science, or ORCID publication profile is recommended to be included as part of the curriculum vitae. The University is committed to attracting and retaining outstanding faculty and staff who will enhance our stature of preeminence in the three missions of teaching, scholarship, and full engagement in our community, the state of Maryland, and the world. Applicants with a research focus on biomanufacturing, biopharmaceuticals, process design/control, and women’s health will be of particular interest, especially those applying machine learning (ML), deep learning (DL), and artificial intelligence (AI) approaches.  However, the faculty search is not limited to these areas, and strong candidates will be considered if their research aligns well with our department. Questions about the position can be directed to the Chair of the Search Committee: umd-chbe-fac-search@umd.edu Financial Disclosure Required No For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department ENGR-Chemical & Biomolecular Engineering Worker Sub-Type Faculty Regular Salary Range 70,000 - 150,000 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Faculty benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UMCP/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Assistant-Professor--Second-Language-Acquisition_JR104839": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Second Language Acquisition",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary Organization's Summary Statement: The Graduate Program in Second Language Acquisition (SLA) in the School of Languages, Literatures, and Cultures (SLLC) at the University of Maryland, College Park, invites applications for a full-time (40 hours) tenure track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor beginning Fall 2027. The area of research specialization within SLA is open, with a preference for second-language processing (e.g., phonological, lexical, syntactic). The successful candidate will be expected to teach two courses per semester and advise graduate students in the candidate’s areas of expertise. In addition, the candidate will be expected to collaborate with other units in SLLC, especially in building the new UG major in Multilingual Applied Studies. The Second Language Acquisition Program seeks a candidate with an innovative scholarly research agenda, a solid background in empirical research, the ability and desire to work on collaborative projects in an interdisciplinary environment, and a commitment to graduate education and open science. We are interested in a candidate whose research promotes the understanding of second language acquisition from cognitive perspectives. We seek candidates whose research, teaching, and service have prepared them to contribute to all of the pillars of the ARHU Strategic Plan: Transformative Thinking; Boundless Creativity; Expansive Empathy; and Meaningful Futures. Contributions toward those goals and values might include leadership in teaching, mentoring, research, or service towards building an equitable and inclusive scholarly environment and/or increasing access or participation of all individuals equitably and fairly. This search is contingent upon the availability of funds. Minimum Qualifications: Education: Ph.D. in SLA or closely related field must be in hand at the time of employment Experience: Evidence of (or demonstrated potential for) a strong publication record Evidence of (or demonstrated potential for) high-quality teaching and mentoring Evidence of (or demonstrated potential for) the potential to obtain extramural funding Knowledge, Skills, Abilities (KSAs) Native or near-native proficiency in English Evidence of strong communication, collaboration, and leadership skills Preferences:  Evidence of classroom teaching experience and research mentoring is desirable. Proficiency or research experience in one or more of the languages taught in the SLLC Additional Job Details Required Application Materials: Cover Letter  Current CV  Research Statement One-page statement of teaching philosophy Sample syllabus for a graduate course Three Writing Samples (published or unpublished research papers) Upload all documents as one PDF After initial screening, candidates will be asked to provide the names and contact information for three references.   Best Consideration Date: October 26, 2026   Posting Close Date: N/A   Open Until Filled: Yes   Financial Disclosure Required No For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department ARHU-School of Languages, Literatures, and Cultures Worker Sub-Type Faculty Regular Salary Range $90,000 - $95,000 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Faculty benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UMCP/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Mid-Senior-Technical-Program-Manager--TPM---Sr-Faculty-Specialist_JR104811": {
      "title": "Mid/Senior Technical Program Manager (TPM)/ Sr. Faculty Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary Organization's Summary Statement: The A. James Clark School of Engineering at the University of Maryland serves as the catalyst for high-quality research, innovation, and learning, delivering on a promise that all graduates will leave ready to impact the Grand Challenges (e.g., energy, environment, security, and human health) of the 21st century. The Clark School is dedicated to leading and transforming the engineering discipline and profession, to accelerating entrepreneurship, and to transforming research and learning activities into new innovations that benefit millions. The Center for Advanced Transportation Technology (CATT) Laboratory is the industry leader for transportation information analysis, visualization, and user interface design. We provide cutting-edge analytics products and an integrated suite of situational awareness tools for transportation practitioners. These products and services are rapidly changing the way governments operate and make decisions. You can learn more about our products at https://ritis.org/. We receive hundreds of gigabytes of transportation data daily, making our petabytes of archived data likely the largest collection of traffic data in the world. Our clients use our software to monitor real-time operations and analyze historical data to generate valuable insights. Our work saves taxpayers money, improves the environment, and saves lives! We’re as passionate about transportation as we are about building great software. We care about building usable, stable, and secure software to analyze massive amounts of data. We use cutting-edge tech to build and maintain our software. We have a mature development process and use industry best practices to build the best software possible. Our team is composed of application developers, analysts, UX designers, data scientists, IT, quality assurance specialists, and customer support operating in an Agile environment. Our office is in College Park near the University of Maryland, easily accessible by DC Metro, MARC train, bus, car, and bike. Local employees are welcome to work in our office, or other locations, with a flexible schedule around our core hours. We also have many employees who are fully remote and work from different states. UMD requires all employees to live in the US, and we periodically bring remote employees to work with colleagues on-site. We believe varied perspectives build better products, are proud to have a diverse team, and encourage people of all backgrounds to apply. When you join our team, you will work to define, document, and test a wide variety of transportation data analytics and operations applications. You will learn new skills and stay current with industry best practices and emerging technologies. Position Summary The Center for Advanced Transportation Technology Laboratory (CATT Lab) is seeking an experienced Mid/Senior Technical Program Manager (TPM) to lead the planning, execution, and delivery of complex software and analytical solutions. The TPM serves as the primary liaison between technical teams, product stakeholders, leadership, and customers to ensure successful delivery of CATT Lab products. This role is responsible for program planning, project execution, stakeholder engagement, and resource coordination across multiple projects and technical disciplines. Approximately 80% of the role focuses on project and program management, with up to 20% dedicated to product ownership responsibilities. The ideal candidate has experience managing multidisciplinary technical teams, quickly learning new programs and technologies, and working effectively in environments with evolving priorities and competing demands. The TPM will oversee one or more of the following technical teams: Software Engineering Data Science and Analytics Data Architecture and Platform UX/UI IT Operations and Infrastructure Customer Support Physical Demands: Sedentary work performed in an office environment. Regularly required to communicate and exchange information and to use technology/devices. Position can be 100% remote (US based only) Minimum Qualifications Master's degree. Five (5) or more years of experience in program management, project management, or product management roles. Experience managing multiple concurrent technical projects or programs with competing priorities. Experience managing complex technical projects involving software development, analytics, data platforms, infrastructure, or operational systems. Experience leading multidisciplinary technical teams with five (5) or more technical resources. Experience communicating technical concepts to both technical and non-technical stakeholders, including executive leadership and customers. Experience with Agile, Scrum, Kanban, or hybrid methodologies. Experience using Jira, Confluence, or comparable tools. Strong communication, facilitation, and stakeholder management skills. Preferences: Bachelor’s or Master's degree in Project Management, Computer Science, Information Systems, Engineering, Analytics, or a related discipline. Eight (8) or more years of experience in program management, project management, or product management roles. Experience serving in both project management and product ownership capacities. Experience managing technical teams delivering software, analytics, or decision-support solutions. Experience with on-premise and/or hybrid infrastructure environments. Demonstrated ability to quickly learn new technologies, business domains, and customer programs. Familiarity with GovRAMP, FedRAMP, NIST 800-53, FISMA, or related security and compliance frameworks. PMP, PMI-ACP, CSM, or comparable certification. Additional Job Details Required Application Materials: CV/Resume Cover Letter (optional) References upon request. Professional Statement-required upon completion of the interview process and before an offer 2 External Letters-required upon completion of the interview process and before an offer Best Consideration date:  9/8/26  Posting close date: Open until filled     Financial Disclosure Required No For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department ENGR-Civil-Center for Advanced Transportation Technology Worker Sub-Type Faculty Regular Salary Range $120,000-$175,000 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Faculty benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UMCP/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Agent-Associate--Agriculture-and-Food-Systems_JR104840": {
      "title": "Agent Associate, Agriculture and Food Systems",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary Organization's Summary Statement: University of Maryland Extension (UME) is a statewide, non-formal education system within the College of Agriculture and Natural Resources and the University of Maryland Eastern Shore. UME educational programs and problem-solving assistance are available to citizens and are based on the research and experience of land grant universities such as the University of Maryland, College Park. In Maryland, UME employs approximately 200 faculty and approximately 200 support staff and contractual employees located at the University of Maryland, College Park; University of Maryland Eastern Shore; 23 counties; Baltimore City; and four research and education centers. Many UME faculty members located on the College Park and Eastern Shore campuses have joint appointments with research and academic programs. These joint appointments promote the exchange of knowledge between the universities and among academic specialties. Position Summary/Purpose of Position: This position is located in the University of Maryland Extension Office in Prince George’s County, Maryland. The position will support the Prince George’s County Agriculture and Food Systems Extension Program. The Educator will provide coordination and programmatic support for agronomy and horticultural crops, livestock, small farm and alternative agriculture, marketing, urban agriculture, and farm and agribusiness development in Prince George’s County, and in collaboration with Extension faculty in the Capitol Cluster. Responsibilities: ● Work with University of Maryland Extension (UME) Agriculture and Food Systems action teams to develop, promote, implement, and evaluate educational programs for agronomic and horticultural crop production, livestock production, small-scale farming and alternative agriculture enterprises, urban agriculture, and farm and agribusiness management to provide educational opportunities for clientele related to agricultural production, business management, and marketing in Prince George’s County, the Capitol Cluster, and across the state. ● Deliver programs in crop production, farm and agribusiness management, integrated pest management, pesticide safety, livestock production, nutrient management, and natural resource conservation for agricultural producers in Prince George’s County, the Capitol Cluster, and across the state. ● Provide training and recertification opportunities for certified private pesticide applicators and nutrient management voucher holders. ● Develop Extension programs that improve the financial viability of farms through business and cooperative development, grain marketing clubs, sustainable agriculture initiatives, community organization, and continuing education for producers. ● Work collaboratively with Maryland-National Capital Park and Planning Commission Prince George's County Planning Department and Southern and Central Maryland Agricultural Marketing Professionals (AMPs) to develop, implement, and evaluate economic development initiatives including, but not limited to, agri-tourism, wholesale markets, direct marketing, and value-added agriculture projects. ● Prepare information for the media, which may include news articles, press releases, and newsletters. ● Remain current in assigned subject matter areas and participate in relevant professional improvement opportunities. ● Develop and implement Extension program marketing and public relations activities. ● Develop grant-funded projects to enhance and expand applied research and educational programs. ● Develop strong relationships with local agriculture organizations, including attendance and participation at Maryland-National Capital Park and Planning Commission Prince George's County Planning Department, Farm Bureau, and Soil Conservation District meetings, as required. ● Develop creative and scholarly activities that are validated by peers and communicated, such as educational materials published and adopted by others, Extension and research publications, conference posters, and professional presentations and participation in applied research. ● Serve as a consultant to county government on the issues of land use, planning, and agriculture and food systems. ● Serve on city, county, and regional agricultural committees. Physical Demands: ● This position frequently presents information through vocal and written communication to individuals of various ages, socio-economic, and educational backgrounds. ● A routine part of this position's responsibilities would be to transport materials to and from field research plots and teaching/event locations, including loading and unloading the vehicle. The employee will frequently lift and/or move items weighing up to 20 pounds. Set up and teardown of research machinery, project displays, and tables and chairs will be necessary at many teaching sites. ● This position requires the employee to work outdoors conducting field research, delivering programs, and teaching at events. This may occur during very hot and/or inclement weather. ● Visual acuity is required for preparing and analyzing written or computer data and presentations. ● Able to traverse farm fields and uneven terrain. Qualifications: Required– ● BS degree in agricultural education, agronomy, animal science, horticulture, agricultural business, or related field and some experience in agricultural rural development or agribusiness. ● Three years of leadership and management experience that demonstrates the ability to work well with farmers and community leaders. ● Knowledge and use of computer technology for educational programming and management. ● Plant diagnostic skills, such as identifying weeds, insects, and diseases. ● Personal transportation and valid driver’s license required. Must be willing to travel throughout the Cluster, as well as the state of Maryland as needed. ● Flexible work schedule required for delivering evening and weekend educational programs and activities as determined by clientele availability and needs. ● Must become a certified Maryland nutrient management advisor/consultant and obtain a commercial pesticide applicators license in category-10 public agency. ● This position is subject to a Criminal History Record Check. Employment is contingent upon successful completion and clearance of the Criminal History Record Check. Preferences: ● M.S. degree in agricultural education, agronomy, animal science, horticulture, agricultural business, or related field. ● Extension or similar work experience in formal or non-formal community-based education. ● Demonstrated ability to acquire grant funding. ● Ability and experience in using social media to engage clientele. Licenses/ Certifications: N/A Additional Job Details Location: This position is located off-campus at the Prince George's County Extension Office in Clinton, MD. Additional Information: Candidate must be eligible to work in the United States at the time of hiring. The department will not provide sponsorship for work-visa requirements. Required Application Materials: All candidates must apply online. A complete application packet must include the following documents: Cover Letter that addresses the applicant's research and Extension experience and philosophies Resume or Curriculum Vitae (CV) Copies of Transcripts Three (3) examples of Extension materials or outputs Three (3) references , each with name, mailing address, telephone number, and email address. Please note that you may upload multiple documents within the same upload field when submitting your application.   Best Consideration Date: 09/30/2026   Posting Close Date: n/a   Open Until Filled: Yes   Financial Disclosure Required No For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department AGNR-UME-Prince George's Worker Sub-Type Faculty Regular Salary Range Bachelors range: $49,809 - $63,809, Masters range: $52,059 - $66,059 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Faculty benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UMCP/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Faculty-Specialist--Agricultural-Nutrient-Management-Program_JR104802": {
      "title": "Faculty Specialist, Agricultural Nutrient Management Program",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary Organization's Summary Statement: Position Summary/Purpose of Position: University of Maryland Extension (UME) seeks candidates for a 12-month professional-track Faculty Specialist position for the Agricultural Nutrient Management Program (ANMP) in the Agriculture and Food Systems (AgFS) Program. The ANMP Faculty Specialist has statewide responsibilities for creating and conducting training programs for farmers, private sector nutrient management plan writers, ANMP nutrient management advisors, and others. The ANMP Faculty Specialist teaches and supports farmers and nutrient management advisors in the development of nutrient management plans that balance nutrient inputs with crop requirements, thus optimizing production potential, improving farm profitability, reducing excess nutrient inputs into the Chesapeake Bay, and enabling producers to comply with Maryland’s Water Quality Improvement Act of 1998. Responsibilities: o Develop Extension guidance documents on agricultural nutrient management topics. o Lead development and instruction of in-person workshops: o Farmer Training and Certification, o How to Write a Nutrient Management Plan, o Fundamentals of Nutrient Management (UMD sections), and o Practical Experiences of Nutrient Management. o Assist farmers and private nutrient management consultants with development of their nutrient management plans remotely and through in-person update sessions. o Train new ANMP nutrient management advisors, mentor them to reach a proficiency in nutrient management plan writing, and provide professional development training on nutrient management topics. o Keep up to date with the latest related research through the scientific literature and attendance at regional and national conferences. o Learn to use and teach the nutrient management software. o Professional development to improve pedagogy. o Attend professional development programs to learn new pedagogy strategies and implement them in ANMP training programs. o Serve on and work collaboratively with UME teams to identify and develop statewide priorities and signature programs for nutrient management. o Serve on program, department, college, and university committees and boards as assigned. Qualifications: Required • Bachelor’s Degree in agronomy, crop science, soil science, or closely related field. • Work experience in agriculture, nutrient management, or closely related area. • Working knowledge of agriculture and farming issues. • Demonstrated teaching abilities. • Strong verbal and written communication skills. • Competency in the use of computer applications (e.g., Word, PowerPoint, Excel, GIS, Google Workspace). • Proven ability to work individually, as a member of a team, and lead a team. • Within one year of employment achieve certification through the Maryland Department of Agriculture as a Nutrient Management Consultant and maintain this certification. • Flexible working hours required; must be available for occasional evening and weekend programs. • A valid driver’s license and access to an automobile for travel. • Evidence of capacity to serve all Marylanders. • This position is subject to a Criminal History Record Check and University of Maryland Background check. Employment is contingent upon successful completion and clearance of the Criminal History Record Check. Preferences: • Master’s Degree in agronomy, crop science, soil science, or closely related field • Experience in agricultural planning. • Certification and experience as a Maryland nutrient management consultant. • Experience with distance education technology (e.g., Canvas, Blackboard) and pedagogy. Physical Demands: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. • Nature of the Position: This position frequently presents information through vocal and written communication to individuals of various ages, socio-economic, and educational backgrounds. • Physical Demands: A routine part of this position's responsibilities would be to transport materials to and from teaching and event locations, including loading and unloading the vehicle. The employee will frequently lift and/or move items weighing up to 20 pounds. Set-up and teardown of displays, tables, and chairs would be necessary at many teaching sites. • Environmental: Team driven, office environment of professional character, competence, and collaboration. Deadline driven in terms of program planning and reporting. This position requires the employee to work outdoors at certain times of the year, especially during the time field research, demonstrations, and meetings are conducted as well as annual county fair. This may occur during very hot and/or inclement weather. • Visual Acuity: Visual acuity is required for preparing and analyzing written or computer data and presentations. Licenses/ Certifications: none Additional Job Details Required Application Materials: All applicants must apply online at UMD Jobs . A complete application packet includes a cover letter, resume, copies of transcripts, and three professional references, including name, mailing address, telephone number, and e-mail address.   Best Consideration Date: 9/27/2026   Posting Close Date: N/A   Open Until Filled: Yes   Financial Disclosure Required No For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department AGNR-UME-Special Agriculture Programs Worker Sub-Type Faculty Regular Salary Range $60,000 to $77,000 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Faculty benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UMCP/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Assistant-Professor_JR104791": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary The Department of Art History and Archaeology at the University of Maryland College Park (UMCP) invites applications for an assistant professor of Early Modern European Art History (1300-1800). Topical and geographical specialty is open. We are particularly interested in scholars with research and teaching interests that complement the Department’s strengths in archaeology and cultural heritage, digital art history, the circulation of objects through trade or conquest, environmental humanities, and histories of race, representation, and colonial power. Candidates are invited to discuss their potential to engage the rich cultural resources of the Washington, D.C.-Maryland-Virginia area in their research and teaching. Successful candidates will demonstrate their readiness to contribute to our undergraduate major and M.A. and Ph.D. programs in Art History and Archaeology through classroom teaching and student mentorship.  Additional Job Details MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Applicants must have completed their doctoral degree in Art History or a related field when the term of appointment commences (July 1, 2027). Teaching experience at the college or university level is required. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS We seek candidates whose research, teaching, and service have prepared them to contribute to all the pillars of the College of Arts and Humanities’ Strategic Plan: Transformative Thinking; Boundless Creativity; Expansive Empathy; and Meaningful Futures. Contributions toward those goals and values might include leadership in teaching, mentoring, research, or service toward building an equitable and inclusive scholarly environment and/or increasing access or participation of all individuals equitably and fairly. REQUIRED APPLICATION MATERIALS (ONLINE): · 3-4-page letter of application (describing scholarly research agenda and teaching philosophy and experience, including proposed courses) · curriculum vitae · writing sample (one article or book/dissertation chapter) · contact information for three recommenders Best consideration date: 10/15/2026 Open Until Filled: Yes Please direct questions to Holly Miller at hmmiller@umd.edu . The Department of Art History and Archaeology is a community of students and scholars that focuses on visual, material and textual expressions as means to understand culture. We critically engage with the reality of living in a world of images, working across a wide range of histories, perspectives and values. Our students at both the undergraduate and graduate levels learn from internationally recognized faculty experts in the field and engage with leading D.C. area arts institutions. Moreover, all students and faculty benefit from innovative technology and digital approaches through the Michelle Smith Collaboratory for Visual Culture.   Financial Disclosure Required For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department ARHU-Art History & Archaeology Worker Sub-Type Faculty Regular Salary Range $90,000 - $95,000 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Faculty benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UMCP/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/ARLIS-Quantum-Research-Professional_JR104818": {
      "title": "ARLIS Quantum Research Professional",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\n\nJob Description Summary Organization's Summary Statement: ARLIS Quantum Research Professional (Open Rank – Faculty Research Specialist, Research Scientist, or Research Engineer) This is an evergreen job posting inviting qualified candidates to apply for current and future roles. Job Description Summary: The Applied Research Laboratory for Intelligence & Security (ARLIS) at the University of Maryland is a University-Affiliated Research Center (UARC) dedicated to advancing research, innovation, and technology transition to improve decision making for U.S. national security. ARLIS combines deep scientific expertise with operational insight to address challenges in intelligence analysis, cybersecurity, artificial intelligence / machine learning, quantum science, and human-machine teaming. Researchers, scientists, engineers, and analysts at ARLIS collaborate with government agencies, industry partners, and academic institutions to deliver actionable insights and transformative solutions through research and development. Employees at ARLIS work on projects of critical importance, contribute directly to the nation’s security, and are supported by a culture that values integrity, collaboration, and professional growth. ARLIS is seeking qualified candidates with expertise in quantum information science to join our multidisciplinary team of research professionals. We invite applicants at all experience levels whose research interests, skills, and backgrounds align with ARLIS’s mission to accelerate applications of quantum technology into operations. Successful candidates will join a growing team of researchers in the Maryland Institute for Quantum Applications (MIQA) at ARLIS. Successful candidates will contribute to a portfolio of government-sponsored projects creating and assessing quantum technology applications related to national intelligence and security. ARLIS is interested in identifying and maturing quantum technologies including quantum sensing & metrology, quantum computing & algorithms, and quantum networking. Positions may include a focus on algorithms development; applications analysis; hardware development, test, and evaluation; literature research and analysis; and systems engineering for quantum technologies. Final appointment title and responsibilities will be based on qualifications and matched to programmatic needs. Roles and Responsibilities: Responsibilities will vary by project and candidate expertise and may include: • Conducting applied research in quantum information science and key supporting technologies. • Critically evaluating the utility of emerging quantum computing, sensing, and networking technologies for DoD and IC applications. • Experimental testing and evaluating of emerging quantum technology products such as optical clocks, magnetometers, and post-quantum cryptography modules. • Supporting workforce development programs to rapidly train quantum-smart professionals for Industry and Government roles. • Collaborating within interdisciplinary teams including professional analysts, software developers, cybersecurity experts, engineers, supply chain experts, and quantum information scientists. • Preparing technical deliverables and briefings for government stakeholders. • Contributing to the preparation of publications, proposals, & technical work plans. Must be able to obtain a U.S. security clearance. If selected, you must meet the requirements for access to classified information and will be subject to a government security clearance investigation that includes criminal and credit history checks, as well as verification of U.S. citizenship, birth, education, employment, and military history. Faculty Research Specialist Track Qualifications: Faculty Research Specialist (Entry Level): Requirements • Bachelor’s degree in Physics, Engineering, Computer Science, Mathematics, or a field closely related to Quantum Information Science. • Experience organizing and managing projects through volunteer, extracurricular, or work activities. • Demonstrated potential for excellence in the execution, administration, and/or management of research or academic programs. • Ability to work collaboratively in a team or work independently with guidance from senior colleagues. • Analytical skills such as scientific programming (Python, Mathematica, etc.), data analysis, statistics, or modeling. Preferred Qualifications: • Excellent verbal and written communication skills • Experience with federal government-sponsored research • Active security clearance Senior Faculty Specialist (Mid Level) Requirements • Master's degree in Physics, Engineering, Computer Science, Mathematics, or a field closely related to Quantum Information Science and 3+ years of experience in a technical role or project management position at the Faculty Research Specialist level; or Bachelor’s Degree and 5+ years of relevant experience in a role of equivalent responsibility • Experience organizing and managing projects through volunteer, extracurricular, or work activities • Experience with federal government-sponsored research • Demonstrated excellence in the execution, administration, and/or management of research or academic programs • Ability to work collaboratively in a team and provide guidance to junior colleagues. • Analytical skills such as scientific programming (Python, Mathematica, etc.), data analysis, statistics, or modeling. Preferred Qualifications: • Excellent verbal and written communication skills • Hands-on experience in quantum technology research and development • Active security clearance Salary Range $80,000 - $134,925 Research Scientist Track Qualifications: Assistant Research Scientist (Entry Level) • PhD in Physics, Engineering, Computer Science, Mathematics, or a field closely related to Quantum Information Science; or an advanced degree with significant research experience in a quantum-related domain in academia, government, or industry. • Evidence of sound scholarly production in Quantum Information Science through publications, presentations, or other scholarly works. • Demonstrated ability to perform research at a level comparable to Assistant Professor. • Expected to begin to apply as a PI for single-investigator proposals and to be Task Leads or Co-PIs on larger proposals. • Professional service contributions such as reviewing journal publications or conference papers, helping to organize conferences, workshops, and researcher visits, conference participation, or professional mentorship. Associate Research Scientist (Mid Level) • PhD in a field closely related to Quantum Information Science plus 5 years of research experience at the Assistant Research Scientist level. • Significant scientific research accomplishments in Quantum Information Science, showing promise of continued productivity, and having the ability to propose, develop, and manage research projects. • Demonstrated ability to perform research at a level comparable to Associate Professor. • Expected to identify funding opportunities with DoD and IC sponsors, and serve as PI or Co-PI on large proposals. • Ability to grow ARLIS and MIQA by mentoring junior researchers and participating in organization sub-committees. • Extensive professional service contributions such as regular service on review panels for funding agencies, academic journal review, conference participation, or professional mentorship. • Experience interfacing regularly with project sponsors or customers. Full Research Scientist (Senior Level) • PhD in a relevant field plus 5 years of research experience at the Associate Research Scientist level. • National or international recognition as a subject matter expert in a field closely related to Quantum Information Science. • Expected to pursue funding opportunities and serve as Principal Investigator or have primary responsibility for a significant part of a multi-investigator project • Serve in a leadership role at ARLIS and MIQA and drive key initiatives and business development opportunities to grow the program • Ability to grow ARLIS and MIQA by mentoring junior and mid-career researchers and leading organization sub-committees. • Extensive professional service contributions such as regular service on review panels for funding agencies, academic journal review, conference participation, or professional mentorship. • Experience leading large, complex engagements with Government sponsor or customers. Salary Range $120,000 - $252,289 Research Engineer Track Qualifications: Assistant Research Engineer (Entry Level) • PhD in an Engineering field related to Quantum Information Science OR a Master’s degree in an Engineering field with 3 years of professional engineering research experience OR a Bachelor’s degree in an Engineering field with 8 years of professional engineering research experience. • Evidence of sound research production in Quantum Information Science through publications, presentations, or successful projects. • Demonstrated ability to perform research at a level comparable to Assistant Professor • Expected to begin to apply as a PI for single-investigator proposals and to be Task Leads or Co-PIs on larger proposals • Professional service may include reviewing journal publications, white papers, statements of work, and proposals; and helping to organize conferences, workshops, and visits by external stakeholders Associate Research Engineer (Mid Level): •PhD in an Engineering field related to Quantum Information Science plus 5 years of research experience at the Assistant Research Engineer level OR a Master’s degree with 8 years of research experience OR a Bachelor’s degree in an Engineering field with 13 years of professional engineering research experience. • Significant scientific research accomplishments in Quantum Information Science, showing promise of continued productivity, and having the ability to propose, develop, and manage research projects. • Demonstrated ability to perform research at a level comparable to Associate Professor. • Expected to identify funding opportunities with DoD and IC sponsors, and serve as PI or Co-PI on large proposals. • Ability to grow ARLIS and MIQA by mentoring junior researchers and participating in organization sub-committees. • Extensive professional service contributions such as regular service on review panels for funding agencies, academic journal review, conference participation, or professional mentorship. • Experience interfacing regularly with project sponsors or customers. Full Research Engineer (Senior Level) • PhD in an Engineering field related to Quantum Information Science plus 5 years of research experience at the Associate Research Engineer level OR a Master’s degree with 13 years of research experience OR a Bachelor’s degree in an Engineering field with 18 years of professional engineering research experience. • National or international recognition as a subject matter expert in a field closely related to Quantum Information Science. • Expected to pursue funding opportunities and serve as Principal Investigator or have primary responsibility for a significant part of a multi-investigator project • Serve in a leadership role at ARLIS and drive key initiatives and business development opportunities to grow the program • Ability to grow ARLIS and MIQA by mentoring junior and mid-career researchers and leading organization sub-committees. • Extensive professional service contributions such as regular service on review panels for funding agencies, academic journal review, conference participation, or professional mentorship. • Experience leading large, complex engagements with Government sponsor or customers Salary Range $110,000 - $240,082 Physical Demands: Sedentary work performed in a normal office environment; exerts up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects, including the human body. Ability to attend meetings both on and off campus. Spending long hours in front of a computer screen. Minimum Qualifications The appointee shall hold a Bachelor’s degree in a relevant area and show potential for excellence in the administration and/or management of academic or research programs. Faculty Specialists are expected to engage in activities such as developing curriculum and/or innovative means for delivering curriculum, supervising the non-research activities of graduate or post-doctoral students, serving as grant writers or authors of other publications for an academic or research program, conducting specialized research duties or other such duties that would generate intellectual property to which the faculty member shall retain the rights. Appointments to this rank are typically one to three years and are renewable. Additional Job Details Required Application Materials: Cover Letter, Resume, List of References   Best Consideration Date: N/A   Posting Close Date: N/A   Open Until Filled: Yes   Department VPR-Applied Research Lab for Intelligence & Security Worker Sub-Type Faculty Regular Salary Range $80,000 - $252,289 Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UMCP/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Faculty-Specialist_JR104783": {
      "title": "Faculty Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary Organization's Summary Statement: Earth System Science Interdisciplinary Center(ESSIC) is a joint center of the University of Maryland and NASA ‘s Goddard Space Flight Center that supports research, teaching and career training in Earth system science. ESSIC also administers the Cooperative Institute for Satellite Earth System Studies (CISESS), a joint center with NOAA’s NCEP and NESDIS that conducts satellite research focused on weather and water forecasting models and predictions. By fostering close integration within the university community and among federal partners at NASA and NOAA, ESSIC serves as a unique collaboration hub within the national Earth System Science research community. POSITION SUMMARY: This position reports to the ESSIC Director and coordinates program development, project delivery and departmental operations by performing a broad range of professional administrative duties in support of the Center Executive Management team. The Faculty Specialist works closely with Center leadership to advance strategic planning, maintain and update organizational documents, coordinate scientific contributions to institutional proposals, coordinate events and initiatives and undertake other assignments as needed. Furthermore, The role coordinates the PTK faculty merit review and promotion processes under the supervision of the ESSIC Associate Director. The role also serves as a liaison for sponsor-related activities, in particular concerning ESSIC’s main Cooperative Agreements with NASA and NOAA. It is anticipated that the role will take on the coordination role for the ESSIC governance structure which is currently being reviewed and updated. Communicates information that requires some explanation or interpretation. Success in this role requires excellent organizational skills and ability to assess and respond effectively to complex and varied situations, interpret and apply policies and procedures, organize and analyze data, and present clear, concise reports. The position also demands sound judgment and discretion in handling sensitive and confidential matters. Physical Demands: Sedentary work. Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects. Repetitive motion. Substantial movements (motions) of the wrists, hands, and/or ﬁngers. The worker is required to have close visual acuity to perform an activity such as: preparing and analyzing data and ﬁgures; transcribing; viewing a computer terminal; extensive reading. Preferences: Licenses/ Certifications: N/A Education: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university with a major in natural sciences required. Master’s degree in field of direct relevance to ESSIC preferred. Qualifications and Experience: •U.S. Citizenship or Green Card holder or applicant from a non-designated country due to restrictions at Government facilities. •Minimum of three years of program management or administrative experience in research and higher education. Knowledge of ESSIC’s main activity areas, its mode of operation and its role in the national landscape of Earth system science an advantage. •Demonstrated ability to collaborate with interdisciplinary teams and coordinate meetings, conferences, and multi-institutional grant proposal activities. •Experience managing projects, including planning, tracking progress, and coordinating deliverables. •Experience leading or coordinating the development of large-scale scientific research proposals involving multiple collaborators. •Familiarity with UMD's Office of Research Administration policies and procedures would be an advantage. Skills and Abilities: •Good skills in oral and written communication. •Skill in the use of Microsoft Office products. •Ability to exercise independent judgment and discretion. •Ability to develop and administer new policies and procedures. •Ability to interpret and apply policies, procedures, regulations, and laws. Additional Job Details Required Application Materials: Cover Letter, curriculum Vitae (CV) and List of References   Best Consideration Date: 09/19/2026   Posting Close Date: N/A   Open Until Filled: Yes   Financial Disclosure Required No For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department CMNS-Earth System Science Interdisciplinary Center Worker Sub-Type Faculty Regular Salary Range Salary Range :$73,940 - $96,637 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Faculty benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UMCP/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Post-Doctoral-Associate_JR104749": {
      "title": "Post-Doctoral Associate",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary Organization's Summary Statement: The Wilkinson lab at the University of Maryland, College Park, is hiring a postdoc to join an ongoing NIH-funded project titled “Social stress, epigenetic and immune function across the bat lifespans.” This project aims to determine if age, reproductive effort or social stress influence immune function and response across the lifespans of males and females from five different species of bats. The postdoc will be responsible for analyzing RNA and DNA methylation sequence data and will assist with sample collection from wild and captive bats. The postdoc will help plan, conduct, and publish research, contribute to the professional development of undergraduate and graduate students, and assist with data dissemination. Physical Demands: This position requires the individual to wear and work in personal protective equipment. This individual may be working with potential biohazards related to animal exposure (airborne allergens, contact reactions) and may be exposed to animal diseases. Minimum Qualifications: A Ph.D. in biology or related field is required by the start date of the appointment. Preferences: Candidates should have a strong background in bioinformatics, genomics and evolutionary biology. A track record of excellent written and verbal communication, and the ability to work well with others is required. Prior experience with analysis of DNA methylation is desirable. Licenses/ Certifications: N/A Additional Job Details Interested candidates should apply through the University of Maryland job portal. Please feel free to email (wilkinso@umd.edu), with \"Post-doctoral position\" in the subject line, before applying to ask questions. This is a one-year appointment with potential for renewal for an additional year. Required Application Materials: 1) Cover letter describing research interests and motivation 2) CV 3) Names and email addresses for 3 references Best Consideration Date: 9/18/2026   Posting Close Date: Until Filled   Open Until Filled: Yes   Financial Disclosure Required No For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department CMNS-Biology Worker Sub-Type Faculty Regular Salary Range $60,000 - $70,000 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Faculty benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UMCP/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Assistant-Professor_JR104738": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary Organization's Summary Statement: The mission of the College of Arts and Humanities (ARHU) is to prepare versatile and visionary leaders equipped to address the complexities of the human experience, both globally and locally. Housed within ARHU, the Department of English teaches students how to think critically, communicate clearly and fearlessly. Equipped with a versatile and interdisciplinary liberal arts education, our students emerge from our classrooms well-prepared to navigate the complex landscape of the current moment. The department’s faculty are premiere in their fields, boasting a body of work that includes award-winning digital media, scholarly essays, novels, short stories and poetry. Our faculty are regular recipients of Guggenheim fellowships, Mellon Foundation grants, NEA awards, NEH fellowships, the Rome Prize, the Whiting Award and American Academy of Arts and Letters awards. The department is an inclusive gathering place for undergraduates, graduate students, faculty and the public. Our Center for Literary and Comparative Studies and BookLab are hubs for scholarly inquiry and partnership with other campus programs and off-campus entities. English regularly hosts readings by poets and novelists; colloquium, symposia, guest lectures and national and international conferences featuring distinguished scholars; as well as discussion groups for students and alumni and play readings and performances. Our majors are encouraged to explore a range of careers through internships, such as with the Maryland General Assembly and the Maryland Institute for Technology in the Humanities. We have a robust alumni program, ensuring continuity between currently enrolled students and those who have gone on to successful careers in marketing, law, medicine, IT, and higher education. Physical Demands: N/A Licenses/ Certifications: N/A Minimum Qualifications: Qualified candidates will have a strong reputation in the field of creative writing with a primary publication record in poetry, at least one full-length poetry book with a nationally recognized publisher, and an MFA in poetry or PhD (preferred) in English literature/creative writing with a focus in poetry. Additional Job Details The Department of English at the University of Maryland, College Park is hiring a tenure-track Assistant Professor of English with a specialization in Poetry to join a thriving creative writing program within a diverse and productive English department to begin in August 2027. Qualified candidates will have a strong reputation in the field of creative writing with a primary publication record in poetry, at least one full-length poetry book with a nationally recognized publisher, and an MFA in poetry or PhD (preferred) in English literature/creative writing with a focus in poetry. The Department seeks a poet who also engages other media forms, genres, and/or secondary studies in literature or art, such as expertise or publications in indigenous studies, digital media, or creative nonfiction. Additional interests are also welcome, such as LGBTQIA+ and trans* literature, African American literature, multiethnic literatures, disability studies, and environmental humanities. An ideal candidate will be experienced in teaching creative writing workshops at the undergraduate/graduate levels, literature courses, and directing undergraduate honors projects or theses. Experience working on, running, or advising students on a literary journal, small press, or experimental or innovative publishing venture would be welcomed. Applicants should have demonstrated ability in working with a varied student body and documented mentorship. The poet’s tenure home will be in the Department of English and they will be a key member of the graduate and undergraduate creative writing programs. Belonging, community, equity, and access drive the mission of the English Department, and we seek candidates whose creative work, teaching, and service have prepared them to contribute to and advance this mission. Within their applications, candidates are asked to summarize their leadership efforts and past or potential contributions to the collegiate community such as leadership in teaching, mentoring, research, or service towards building an equitable and varied scholarly environment and/or increasing access or participation of individuals from equity-deserving groups.  Best consideration date is October 15, 2026.  Applications will be accepted and reviewed until the position is filled.  The University of Maryland is located in College Park, eight miles from the heart of Washington, DC, and served by the Washington Metro System, offering its faculty access to world-class library and archival facilities, an array of cultural institutions, and culturally and linguistically diverse communities.  The MFA Program in Creative Writing is staffed by a stellar faculty, active on the national and international literary scene, with strong ties to the greater D.C. literary arts community.  We are committed to belonging and community and run a vibrant program grounded in mentoring of young writers.  MFA alumni are noted for their award-winning publications with independent and major presses, for continuing their graduate education at top-tier doctoral programs, and for starting their own nationally recognized journals and magazines.   UMD will not sponsor the successful candidate for work authorization in the United States now or in the future. Required Application Materials: - Letter of application - Curriculum Vitae - 1 page creative/research statement - 1 page teaching philosophy statement - 1 page statement summarizing your leadership efforts, past or potential contributions to belonging, community, equity and access - 10 page representative writing sample Candidates should be prepared to provide three letters of recommendation, which the committee will request at a more advanced stage of the search process.   Best Consideration Date: 10/15/2026   Posting Close Date: N/A   Open Until Filled: Yes   Financial Disclosure Required No For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department ARHU-English Worker Sub-Type Faculty Regular Salary Range $90,000-$95,000 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Faculty benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UMCP/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Lecturer_JR104676": {
      "title": "Lecturer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary & Additional Information The Artificial Intelligence Interdisciplinary Institute at Maryland (AIM; aim.umd.edu) has openings for instructional faculty positions to teach in its Bachelor of Science (BS) in AI program, which focuses on technical foundations of AI in addition to exposing students to interdisciplinary applications and societal implications of AI. These openings are for Professional Track Faculty (non-tenure track) positions. All Professional Track Faculty members in AIM will work with our bright and amazing students and play a key role in teaching our artificial intelligence curricula. As members of AIM, successful applicants will join and help further our mission of defining and engaging in interdisciplinary AI education across all of the UMD College Park campus, and in building a thriving and inclusive AI community. Strong candidates will be considered in all areas of AI that align with AIM’s BS in AI program. The BS in AI is a highly technical program that trains students to build new AI systems and algorithms from the ground up, understand the training of models from both a data and systems perspective, and then use those techniques in interdisciplinary applications. Specializations will include: Generative AI; AI, Society, and Decision Making; AI Algorithms; Accessibility; and Robotics. We are especially looking for candidates that are interested in actively participating in a strong community of AI-related scholars across disciplines. The successful candidate will hold an M.S. degree (Ph.D. preferred) in computer science or a related field. Courses to be Taught: CMSC141 Programming with Purpose I: Data-Centric Computing, CMSC142 Data Structures and Algorithms, CSAI216 Efficient Systems for AI Applications, CSAI220 Measuring Preferences and Rankings, CSAI221 Classical AI Algorithms Physical Demands: Normal classroom teaching demands. Preferences: Candidates with a PhD and a willingness to teach advanced upper-level courses in the candidate’s area of specialization.   Required Application Materials: CV, cover letter, teaching portfolio   Best Consideration Date: 9/11/2026   Posting Close Date:   Open Until Filled: Yes   Department CMNS-AIM Worker Sub-Type Faculty Non-Regular (Fixed Term) Salary Range $35,907 - $101,193 Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UMCP/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Assistant-Professor_JR104513": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary Organization's Summary Statement: Human beings share a capacity for language, unique to the species. This capacity guides the learning of language in children and constrains the character of the languages we come to have. To study it we pursue various sources of evidence. Among them are the grammars of individual languages; patterns of grammatical variation across languages; the development, normal and abnormal, of language in children; the mental processing of language in use; and the embodiment of language in the brain. But all these perspectives converge on a single natural object: the human language faculty, whose study unifies the work at Maryland Linguistics. The Department of Linguistics at the University of Maryland combines current theoretical research in phonology, syntax, and semantics with state-of-the-art experimental research in language acquisition, computational linguistics, psycholinguistics and neurolinguistics, in order to understand the human capacity for language. Connections between our core competencies are strong, with theoretical, experimental and computational work typically pursued in tandem. A network of collaboration at all levels sustains a research climate that is both vigorous and friendly. Here new ideas develop in conversation, stimulated by the steady activity of our labs and research groups, frequent student meetings with faculty, regular talks by local and invited scholars and collaborations with a campus community of over 200 language scientists. Position Summary/Purpose of Position: The Linguistics Department at the University of Maryland, College Park invites applications for an Assistant Professor of Syntax with an anticipated starting date of August 8, 2027. Applicants should be prepared to teach courses at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. We seek to hire someone with an active research program, who is prepared to work closely with graduate students, and whose research connects with existing strengths in linguistic theory, psycholinguistics and computational linguistics. The expected teaching load is four courses per year (2-2). Applicants must have a PhD (Linguistics, Cognitive Science, or allied fields) or expect to have one before the start date. As an Assistant Professor you will: - Teach courses at both the undergraduate and graduate level. - Work closely with graduate students. - Conduct research in syntactic theory. - Participate in shared governance of the department, college, and university. We seek candidates whose research, teaching and service have prepared them to contribute to diversity and inclusion. Minimum Qualifications: In compliance with the University System of Maryland Policy on Appointment, Rank, and Tenure of Faculty and the College of Arts and Humanities Tenure Track Faculty Appointment, Evaluation, and Promotion Procedures, the Department of Linguistics' minimum criteria for appointment of tenure track faculty is: Education and Experience: - A Ph.D, in Linguistics or a related field. Criteria for evaluating candidates will include the following: - Evidence of an active research program in syntax. - Evidence of success in teaching and mentoring undergraduate students. Physical Demands: - Ability to deliver lectures in a large classroom setting, which may require walking between campus buildings. - Ability to operate standard office equipment and keyboards. Licenses/ Certifications: N/A Additional Job Details Preferences: - Candidates with a demonstrated ability to incorporate diverse perspectives in their teaching. - Candidates whose research engages with a diversity of data types, possibly including field work, corpus data, experimental syntax, psycholinguistics, language acquisition. Required Application Materials: - An application letter. - A current CV. - A research statement. - A teaching statement. - A statement of Contributions to Diversity. - Three writing samples. - The names and contact information for three references.   In their application letter, candidates should briefly describe their research program, their teaching experience and their experience with diversity. Best Consideration Date: December 15, 2026   Posting Close Date: N/A   Open Until Filled: Yes   Financial Disclosure Required No For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department ARHU-Linguistics Worker Sub-Type Faculty Regular Salary Range $95,000 - $100,000 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Faculty benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UMCP/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Maryland-Quantum-NEXUS_JR104672": {
      "title": "Maryland Quantum NEXUS",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\n\nJob Description Summary Organization's Summary Statement: The Applied Research Laboratory for Intelligence & Security (ARLIS) at the University of Maryland is a University-Affiliated Research Center (UARC) dedicated to advancing research, innovation, and technology transition to improve decision making for U.S. national security. ARLIS combines deep scientific expertise with operational insight to address challenges in intelligence analysis, cybersecurity, artificial intelligence / machine learning, quantum science, and human-machine teaming. Researchers, scientists, engineers, and analysts at ARLIS collaborate with government agencies, industry partners, and academic institutions to deliver actionable insights and transformative solutions through research and development. Employees at ARLIS work on projects of critical importance, contribute directly to the nation’s security, and are supported by a culture that values integrity, collaboration, and professional growth. Maryland Quantum NEXUS is ARLIS's quantum workforce development initiative required by the Capital Quantum Benchmarking Hub MOU signed between DARPA and the State of Maryland. It is designed to build the next generation of talent for Maryland's quantum ecosystem. By connecting emerging quantum professionals with applied research, industry, government, and national security partners NEXUS develops workforce-ready professionals to support DARPA’s Quantum Benchmarking Initiative and meet Maryland's growing quantum workforce needs while strengthening the state's leadership in quantum innovation. Maryland Quantum NEXUS focuses on training technicians for practical work in qubit modalities including neutral atom, solid-state superconducting, solid-state semiconducting, and topological. The program is intended to recruit and develop early-career talent through a structured, multi-rotation model that combines hands-on project experience with mentorship and targeted professional development. The goal is to support participants in progressing from foundational technical knowledge to the applied skills and competencies required to contribute effectively in quantum research and industry environments. We train technicians – not researchers, turning undergraduates and those with professional experience into quantum technicians and engineers. Our program focuses less on theory, advanced mathematics, and research practice and more on the day-to-day mix of hardware, software, and experimental skills needed to run quantum systems. Set up, tear down, and reconfigure labs. Calibrate instruments and evaluate results. Must be able to obtain a US security clearance. If selected, must meet the requirements for access to classified information and will be subject to a government security clearance investigation that includes criminal and credit history checks, as well as verification of U.S. citizenship, birth, education, employment, and military history. Final offer is contingent upon the candidate’s ability to successfully obtain the necessary interim Secret security clearance, as determined by ARLIS, prior to commencing employment. Minimum Qualifications: Education: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited university. Experience: Three years of experience in a science, engineering, or laboratory environment. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: - Familiarity with coding and programming practices. - Skill in the use of Microsoft Office products. - Skill in troubleshooting errors and fault-finding. - Ability to multi-task and prioritize assignments. - Ability to analyze situations and determine the best recourse for response. - Physical Demands: - Light work, splitting time between an office environment and a quantum laboratory environment. - Exerts 21 to 35 pounds of force occasionally, and/or 13 to 21 pounds of force frequently, and/or greater than negligible up to 7-10 pounds of force constantly to move objects. - Ability to attend meetings and events both on and off campus. When in office spending long hours in front of a computer screen. When in the lab requires walking or standing to a significant degree with periodic (monthly) tear down and rebuild of scientific equipment. Application Submission Requirements: Please carefully review the required application materials listed in this post and ensure that all requested documents are included with your submission. Incomplete applications or applications missing required documentation may not receive full consideration. Preferences: - Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Electrical Engineering, Chemical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Electronics, Physics, Mathematics, Chemistry & Materials, or Quantum Technologies with two (2) years experience in a science, engineering, or laboratory environment. - Able to operate basic test and measurement devices (e.g., power supplies, multimeters). - Assembly, test, or calibration of electronic systems and components. - Able to do basic troubleshooting using an iterative and logical approach. - General practical experimental skills acquired through research experiences or lab coursework. - Able to interpret computational or measurement results to understand physical systems. - Programming experience with Python or Go for data processing, data visualization / representation, or other purposes. - Able to troubleshoot code or use a debugger. - Able to use computers to collect and process data. - Able to perform data analysis, including uncertainty analysis. - Able to integrate multiple scientific principles when designing experiments. - Able to integrate multiple scientific principles to translate findings into practical applications. - Able to prepare and deliver presentations to multiple stakeholders. - Able to collaborate effectively with others. - Able to think critically (e.g., critical assessment of their own work and that of others to identify strengths and limitations). - Comfort working independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced, evolving environment. - Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. - Active security clearance or eligibility. Licenses/ Certifications: N/A Minimum Qualifications Additional Job Details Required Application Materials: Cover Letter, Resume, List of References   Best Consideration Date: N/A   Posting Close Date: N/A   Open Until Filled: Yes   Department VPR-Applied Research Lab for Intelligence & Security Worker Sub-Type Faculty Regular Salary Range $75,000 - $85,000 Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UMCP/job/ANNE-ARUNDEL-COUNTY-EXTENSION-BUILDING/Agent-Associate--Home-Horticulture-Educator---Master-Gardener_JR104592": {
      "title": "Agent Associate, Home Horticulture Educator & Master Gardener",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-07\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary Organization's Summary Statement: University of Maryland Extension (UME) is a statewide, non-formal education system within the College of Agriculture and Natural Resources and the University of Maryland Eastern Shore. UME educational programs and problem-solving assistance are available to citizens and are based on the research and experience of land grant universities such as the University of Maryland, College Park. In Maryland, UME employs approximately 200 faculty and approximately 200 support staff and contractual employees located at the University of Maryland, College Park; University of Maryland Eastern Shore; 23 counties; Baltimore City; and four research and education centers. Many UME faculty members located on the College Park and Eastern Shore campuses have joint appointments with research and academic programs. These joint appointments promote the exchange of knowledge between the universities and among academic specialties. Position Summary/Purpose of Position: This is a full-time position that will work in support of the Anne Arundel County Home Horticulture Extension Programs. The Faculty Extension Educator will administer all aspects of the Anne Arundel’s County horticulture programs which includes coordination and programmatic support for home horticulture education and activities in both counties, training and management of Master Gardener Volunteers, collaboration on educational programs among partners, outreach to clientele, and marketing. Responsibilities: • Develop, conduct, and evaluate educational seminars, classes, workshops, and other presentations related to home horticulture. • Create educational products based on stakeholder needs including fact sheets and other publications, and other content for social media and websites (blogs, videos and pod casts, etc.) • Manage the Master Gardener Program in the county which includes volunteer recruitment, training, supervision and developing collaborations for community-based projects. • Respond to clientele requests via phone, office visits, email, etc., for general horticulture information pertaining to lawn care, landscape plants and trees, composting, native plants, pest control, and other subject related to home horticulture, providing appropriate literature and advice in a timely and professional manner. • Identify plants, insects, and other horticulture samples submitted by clientele and respond with information and recommendations in a timely and professional manner. • Provide pest control and fertilizer recommendations in accordance with University of Maryland guidelines. • Disseminate horticulture information to residents of both counties through news releases, website updates, etc. • Assist in collecting, reporting and evaluating impact data of local home horticulture programs in accordance with funding requirements and UMD/UME policies and protocols. • Develop and maintain collaborative relationships with community and other relevant organizations to implement and evaluate programs, and seek new partnerships, especially to reach traditionally underserved or marginalized audiences to deliver outreach education. • Collaborate with other UME field- and campus-based faculty and staff on programs and projects of mutual interest when and where appropriate. • Provide supervision and mentoring for the Master Gardener extension program assistant. • Participate in committees and other service opportunities at the county, state and University level. Physical Demands: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. • Nature of the Position: This position frequently presents information through verbal and written communication to individuals of various ages, socio-economic, and educational backgrounds. The ability to express or exchange ideas verbally is important, as well as the ability to hear and perceive information at normal spoken work levels. • Physical Demands: A routine part of this position's responsibilities would be to transport materials to and from teaching/event locations, including loading and unloading the vehicle. The employee will frequently lift and/or move items weighing up to 20 pounds. Set-up and tear-down of displays, tables, and chairs would be necessary at many teaching sites. • Environmental: Primary work will occur in an office, but the employee will also be working in gardens, farms, and other outdoor conditions in course of developing demonstration sites, delivering programs, and teaching at events. This may occur during very hot and/or inclement weather. • Visual acuity: Visual acuity is required for driving, preparing and analyzing written or computer data, and preparing presentations, and identifying plants and pests. Qualifications: Required- • Bachelor’s Degree in horticulture, agriculture education, applied plant science, agronomy or related field. • A minimum of one year working in horticulture, agriculture, agronomy or related fields or a combination of education and training providing the required knowledge, skills and abilities. • Demonstrated leadership and management abilities. • Working knowledge of accepted home horticulture practices. • Ability to work independently with limited guidance and instruction. • Self-motivated, flexible, innovative, and resourceful. • Experience working with volunteers. • Willingness to work with a variety of audiences reflecting all socio-economic perspectives. • Ability to communicate effectively, both orally and in writing. • Knowledge and use of computer technology for educational programming and management. • Availability to work flexible hours; including evening and weekend programs and meetings. • Valid driver's license and access to an automobile for travel. • This position is subject to a Criminal History Record Check and University of Maryland Background check. Employment is contingent upon successful completion and clearance of the Criminal History Record Check. Preferences: • Master’s Degree in horticulture, agriculture education, applied plant science, agronomy or related field. • 2 or more years of experience working in horticulture, agriculture, agronomy or related fields or a combination of education and training providing the required knowledge, skills and abilities • Experience in program planning, conducting and delivering community-based programs and conducting collaborative work with other organizations • Experience in writing grants and securing funds for projects Licenses/ Certifications: N/A Additional Job Details Location: This position is located off-campus at the Anne Arundel County Extension Office in Gambrills, MD. Additional Information: Candidate must be eligible to work in the United States at the time of hiring. The department will not provide sponsorship for work-visa requirements. Required Application Materials: A complete application packet must include the following documents: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae (CV) Copies of Transcripts Three (3) references , each with name, mailing address, telephone number, and email address. Please note that you may upload multiple documents within the same upload field when submitting your application. Best Consideration Date: 9/7/2026   Posting Close Date: n/a   Open Until Filled: Yes   Financial Disclosure Required No For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department AGNR-UME-Anne Arundel Worker Sub-Type Faculty Regular Salary Range Bachelor’s hiring range: $49,809 - $63,809, Master’s hiring range: $52,059 - $66,059 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Faculty benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UMCP/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Assistant-Professor_JR104554": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary ORGANIZATION'S SUMMARY STATEMENT: The Department of Kinesiology within the School of Public Health at the University of Maryland College Park (https://sph.umd.edu/academics/departments-units/department-kinesiology) invites applications for a 9-month tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor. The department is seeking a highly motivated and collaborative scientist in the area of biomechanics. Applicants for this position should have strong potential for research excellence in the understanding of mechanical, neuromuscular, and/or computational mechanisms underlying human movement across the lifespan. Applicants with research foci in the areas of musculoskeletal biomechanics, neuromechanics, injury and rehabilitation, wearable sensing, movement analytics, and/or biomechanics of aging and disease are encouraged to apply. The successful candidate will be expected to establish and sustain a high-quality, extramurally funded research program, teach undergraduate and graduate courses in biomechanics and related areas, advise and mentor graduate students, and serve on comprehensive examination committees and department committees. Special consideration will be given to candidates who complement ongoing research within the department. PURPOSE OF POSITION: The Department of Kinesiology embodies the core pillars of the University of Maryland’s Strategic Plan by advancing innovative research, reimagining learning, and addressing grand challenges in human health and performance. The department examines the complex role of physical activity and movement in health and well-being across the lifespan through interdisciplinary collaboration and research. The University of Maryland is the flagship institution of the state of Maryland on the ancestral lands of the Piscataway people, the traditional stewards of the lands where we work, live, and learn. The University of Maryland is an extraordinary place—vibrant and dynamic and diverse. We are a place of learning: a school dedicated to the art and science of education and committed to reimagining teaching and learning inside both classrooms and communities. We are a campus dedicated to the indisputable value of science and humanities, inquiry, and creativity, and comprising thousands of researchers and discoverers working in hundreds of laboratories, libraries, and collaborative spaces. Strategically located just a few miles from the US capital, our university is a place where new knowledge is pursued, discovered, and championed. We are also a community, nearly half a million members strong, of diverse students, faculty, staff, and alumni; a small city of residents and commuters, first responders and health care workers, learners, artists, and athletes; a place where thousands come to work every day to make a difference. Our diversity is integral to our excellence. And, ours is a community that is intrinsically connected to our surrounding neighborhoods and our state, our nation, and our world. The University of Maryland remains, since our founding, an institution of change and progress dedicated to the public good. Our university is evolving faster than at any moment in its storied history. Our guiding principles are helping us to empower the next generation of leaders, educators, scientists, and global citizens to develop creative solutions to the grand challenges of our times. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Education: Candidates should possess a doctoral degree in kinesiology, biomechanics, biomedical engineering, mechanical engineering, exercise science, or a closely related field. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Demonstrated expertise in the biomechanics of human movement. Evidence of (or demonstrated potential for) a sustainable and focused research program. Evidence of experience with advanced laboratory (clinical, basic, biomechanical, or computational) methodologies Evidence of (or demonstrated potential for) a strong publication record in kinesiology. Evidence of (or demonstrated potential for) high-quality teaching and mentoring in kinesiology. Evidence of strong communication, collaboration, and leadership skills within a research team. Preferences: Postdoctoral research experience is strongly preferred. There should be evidence of the potential to obtain extramural funding. Evidence of classroom teaching experience and research mentoring is desirable. PHYSICAL DEMANDS: No unusual physical or environmental demands Normal classroom teaching demands Using a computer and keyboard Sitting for periods of time Standing for periods of time Using lab or mechanical equipment LICENSES/CERTIFICATIONS: N/A Additional Job Details Required Application Materials: Cover letter describing interests, qualifications, and current research Curriculum vitae Three representative publications that are illustrative of their research expertise List of three references (letters not required at time of application) Applications will be held in confidence until finalists are invited for campus interviews. References will not be contacted without a candidate’s consent.   Review of applications will begin on October 16, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Best Consideration Date: 10/16/2026   Posting Close Date: N/A   Open Until Filled: Yes   Financial Disclosure Required No For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department SPHL-Kinesiology Worker Sub-Type Faculty Regular Salary Range $100,000-$110,000 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Faculty benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
    },
    "https://umd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UMCP/job/University-of-Maryland-College-Park/Post-Doctoral-Associate_JR104531": {
      "title": "Post Doctoral Associate",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-29\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary Organization's Summary Statement: Postdoctoral Research Opportunity – Energy Transport and Conversion University of Maryland The Energy Transport and Ultrafast Spectroscopy Lab at the University of Maryland is seeking a Postdoctoral Researcher to work on cutting-edge projects in nano/macro-scale energy transport and conversion. The successful candidate will play a key role in advancing experimental and/or computational approaches to address grand challenges in energy science and engineering. 🔗 Learn more about our research: Energy Transport Lab The A. James Clark School of Engineering at the University of Maryland serves as a catalyst for high-quality research, innovation, and learning, preparing our students to develop innovations that address the 21st-century Grand Challenges (e.g., energy, environment, security, and human health) and improve the human condition. The Clark School is dedicated to leading and transforming the engineering discipline and profession, accelerating entrepreneurship, and transforming research and learning activities into innovations that benefit millions. Responsibilities: • Conduct independent and collaborative research on thermal/energy transport at multiple length scales. • Develop and apply advanced experimental thermometries and/or computational models. • Mentor graduate and undergraduate students. Minimum Qualifications: • PhD in Mechanical Engineering, Materials Science, Physics, or a related field. • Strong background in thermal sciences, heat transfer, or energy systems. • Demonstrated research productivity (journal publications, conference presentations). • Excellent communication and teamwork skills. Position Details: • Full-time, funded position with competitive salary and benefits. • Initial appointment of 1 year, renewable based on performance and funding. How to Physical Demands: N/A Preferences: Experience with computational tools (e.g., molecular dynamics, first-principles calculations) and/or experimental methods (e.g., thermal metrology, materials characterization, pump-probe measurements) is highly desirable. Licenses/ Certifications: N/A Additional Job Details Required Application Materials: Cover letter, CV, List of references   Best Consideration Date: 08/15/2026   Posting Close Date: N/A   Open Until Filled: Yes   Financial Disclosure Required No For more information on Financial Disclosure, please visit Maryland's State Ethics Commission website . Department ENGR-Mechanical Engineering PM Worker Sub-Type Faculty Regular Salary Range $60,000 - $65,000 Benefits Summary For more information on Regular Faculty benefits, select this link . Background Checks Offers of employment are contingent on completion of a background check. Information reported by the background check will not automatically disqualify anyone from employment. Before any adverse decision, the finalist will have an opportunity to provide information to the University regarding disclosable background check information. The University reserves the right to rescind the offer of employment or otherwise decline or terminate employment if the information reported by the background check is deemed incompatible with the position, regardless of when the background check is completed. Employment Eligibility The successful candidate must complete employment eligibility verification (on Form I-9) by presenting documents that establish identity and work authorization within the timeframe required by federal immigration law, and where applicable, to demonstrate renewed employment authorization.  Failure to complete employment eligibility verification or reverification within the timeframe set forth by law may result in suspension or termination of employment. EEO Statement The University of Maryland, College Park is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. Please read the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity Statement of Policy. Title IX Non-Discrimination Notice Resources Learn how military skills translate to civilian opportunities with  O*Net Online Search Firm Managed Recruitment There are some positions that are not advertised on this career site as the search is being managed by a Search Firm. Please visit the link below to see these available opportunities: Search Firm Managed Vacancies"
